               <math id="alg2.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{k+1}\leftarrow\textsc{CappedHalfTurn}(X_{k},Y_{k+1},\widetilde{X},\bar{\lambda})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">CappedHalfTurn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{k+1}\leftarrow\textsc{CappedHalfTurn}(X_{k},Y_{k+1},\widetilde{X},\bar{\lambda})</annotation></semantics></math>
using <a href="#alg1a" title="In 4.2 Simulating the half-turn process ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>

