            <span id="alg2.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Choice of parameters.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,1/4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,1/4)</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leq 1/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leq 1/\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, and a tuning constant <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\coloneqq K\,\Bigl[\Delta+\log\Bigl(\frac{Kd\kappa}{\varepsilon\alpha\eta}\Bigr)\Bigr]\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\bar{\lambda}_{\rm impl}\coloneqq K\beta\eta\,(\sqrt{d\ell}+\ell)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.150em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>impl</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\coloneqq K\,\Bigl[\Delta+\log\Bigl(\frac{Kd\kappa}{\varepsilon\alpha\eta}\Bigr)\Bigr]\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\bar{\lambda}_{\rm impl}\coloneqq K\beta\eta\,(\sqrt{d\ell}+\ell)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Set <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> as in (<a href="#S3.E12" title="Equation 3.12 ‣ Theorem 3.5 (𝜒^2 convergence). ‣ 3.3 Ideal Proximal BPS ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.12</span></a>), let <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> be the smallest
integer satisfying (<a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 3.13 ‣ Theorem 3.5 (𝜒^2 convergence). ‣ 3.3 Ideal Proximal BPS ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.13</span></a>), and define</p>
<table id="S4.E9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E9X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E9X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E9X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\Bigl\lceil K\,\Bigl(\Delta+\log\frac{4}{\varepsilon}\Bigr)\Bigr\rceil\,N\,,\hskip 20.00003pta\coloneqq\frac{\varepsilon}{6T}\,,\hskip 20.00003ptQ_{\rm prox}\coloneqq\bigl\lceil K\log(\kappa\ell)\bigr\rceil\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≔</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⌈</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em" stretchy="true">⌉</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>prox</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⌈</mo><mi>K</mi><mi>log</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⌉</mo><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\Bigl\lceil K\,\Bigl(\Delta+\log\frac{4}{\varepsilon}\Bigr)\Bigr\rceil\,N\,,\hskip 20.00003pta\coloneqq\frac{\varepsilon}{6T}\,,\hskip 20.00003ptQ_{\rm prox}\coloneqq\bigl\lceil K\log(\kappa\ell)\bigr\rceil\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(4.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.3</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Sampler from an order-2 Rényi warm start)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist universal constants <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> such
that the following holds. Assume (<a href="#S1.E1" title="Equation 1.1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>). Let
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,1/4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,1/4)</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be a
probability measure on <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{2}(\mu_{0}\|\mu)\leq\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{2}(\mu_{0}\|\mu)\leq\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, and choose <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leq 1/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leq 1/\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume that</span></p>
<table id="S4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\,\bigl(\sqrt{d\ell}+\ell\bigr)\leq c\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\,\bigl(\sqrt{d\ell}+\ell\bigr)\leq c\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Run <a href="#alg2a" title="In 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> from <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}\sim\mu_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}\sim\mu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> using
(<a href="#S4.E8" title="Equation 4.8 ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a>)–(<a href="#S4.E9" title="Equation 4.9 ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.9</span></a>). If
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is its output and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\nabla V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\nabla V}</annotation></semantics></math> is its total number
of gradient queries, then</span></p>
<table id="S4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{TV}\bigl(\mathcal{L}(\widehat{X}),\mu\bigr)\leq\varepsilon\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{TV}\bigl(\mathcal{L}(\widehat{X}),\mu\bigr)\leq\varepsilon\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, its expected query count satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S4.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}N_{\nabla V}\leq\frac{K}{\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}\sqrt{\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\,\Bigl(\Delta+\log\frac{4}{\varepsilon}\Bigr)\,\bigl[Q_{\rm prox}+\beta\eta\,\bigl(\sqrt{d\ell}+\ell\bigr)\bigr]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>K</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}N_{\nabla V}\leq\frac{K}{\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}\sqrt{\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\,\Bigl(\Delta+\log\frac{4}{\varepsilon}\Bigr)\,\bigl[Q_{\rm prox}+\beta\eta\,\bigl(\sqrt{d\ell}+\ell\bigr)\bigr]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{0}\coloneqq\mathcal{L}(X_{0},Y_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{0}\coloneqq\mathcal{L}(X_{0},Y_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. By
(<a href="#S2.E18" title="Equation 2.18 ‣ 2.3 Divergences and notation ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.18</span></a>) and (<a href="#S2.E16" title="Equation 2.16 ‣ 2.3 Divergences and notation ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.16</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{2}(\nu_{0}\|\pi_{\eta})\leq\Delta\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\chi^{2}(\nu_{0}\|\pi_{\eta})\leq e^{\Delta}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{2}(\nu_{0}\|\pi_{\eta})\leq\Delta\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\chi^{2}(\nu_{0}\|\pi_{\eta})\leq e^{\Delta}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, (<a href="#S4.E10" title="Equation 4.10 ‣ Theorem 4.3 (Sampler from an order-2 Rényi warm start). ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a>) gives
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\sqrt{d}\leq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\sqrt{d}\leq c</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leq c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leq c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and using
(<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 3.15 ‣ Theorem 3.5 (𝜒^2 convergence). ‣ 3.3 Ideal Proximal BPS ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.15</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{TV}\bigl((\nu_{0}\mathcal{K}^{T})^{X},\mu\bigr)\leq\frac{1}{2}\exp\Bigl\{\frac{1}{2}\,\Bigl[\Delta-\Bigl\lceil K\,\Bigl(\Delta+\log\frac{4}{\varepsilon}\Bigr)\Bigr\rceil\Bigr]\Bigr\}\leq\frac{\varepsilon}{2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>X</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{TV}\bigl((\nu_{0}\mathcal{K}^{T})^{X},\mu\bigr)\leq\frac{1}{2}\exp\Bigl\{\frac{1}{2}\,\Bigl[\Delta-\Bigl\lceil K\,\Bigl(\Delta+\log\frac{4}{\varepsilon}\Bigr)\Bigr\rceil\Bigr]\Bigr\}\leq\frac{\varepsilon}{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">after increasing <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. Minimality of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, together with
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\eta\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\eta\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.E13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E13X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E13X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E13X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 1+\frac{C}{\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}\sqrt{\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\leq\frac{C+1}{\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}\sqrt{\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 1+\frac{C}{\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}\sqrt{\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\leq\frac{C+1}{\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}\sqrt{\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(4.13)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E13Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E13Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E13Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{C}{\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}\sqrt{\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\,\Bigl(\Delta+\log\frac{4}{\varepsilon}\Bigr)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{C}{\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}\sqrt{\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\,\Bigl(\Delta+\log\frac{4}{\varepsilon}\Bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{k}\coloneqq\nu_{0}\mathcal{K}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{k}\coloneqq\nu_{0}\mathcal{K}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{k}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{k}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> be its image
under the reflection at the start of transition <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> preserves <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> and the reflection is a
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>-preserving bijection, data processing gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{2}(\nu_{k}^{+}\|\pi_{\eta})=D_{2}(\nu_{k}\|\pi_{\eta})\leq D_{2}(\nu_{0}\|\pi_{\eta})\leq\Delta\,,\hskip 20.00003pt0\leq k&lt;T\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{2}(\nu_{k}^{+}\|\pi_{\eta})=D_{2}(\nu_{k}\|\pi_{\eta})\leq D_{2}(\nu_{0}\|\pi_{\eta})\leq\Delta\,,\hskip 20.00003pt0\leq k&lt;T\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{-1}=6T/\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{-1}=6T/\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, (<a href="#S4.E13" title="Equation 4.13 ‣ Proof. ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.13</span></a>) and
(<a href="#S4.E6" title="Equation 4.6 ‣ Item (i) ‣ Proposition 4.2 (Capped-rate approximation and query cost). ‣ 4.2 Simulating the half-turn process ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a>) yield, for a sufficiently large universal <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;a&lt;\frac{1}{2}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\log\frac{1}{a}\vee\ell_{a,\Delta}\leq C\,\Bigl[\Delta+\log\Bigl(\frac{Kd\kappa}{\varepsilon\alpha\eta}\Bigr)\Bigr]\leq\ell\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;a&lt;\frac{1}{2}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\log\frac{1}{a}\vee\ell_{a,\Delta}\leq C\,\Bigl[\Delta+\log\Bigl(\frac{Kd\kappa}{\varepsilon\alpha\eta}\Bigr)\Bigr]\leq\ell\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leq\min\{c_{0},c_{\rm evt},K_{\rm RGO}^{-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>evt</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>RGO</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leq\min\{c_{0},c_{\rm evt},K_{\rm RGO}^{-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq K_{\rm evt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>evt</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq K_{\rm evt}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}&amp;K_{\rm RGO}\beta\eta\,\bigl\{\sqrt{d\log(1/a)}+\log(1/a)\bigr\}\leq K_{\rm RGO}c\leq 1\,,\\
&amp;\bar{\lambda}_{\rm impl}=K\beta\eta\,(\sqrt{d\ell}+\ell)\geq K_{\rm evt}\beta\eta\,(\sqrt{d\ell_{a,\Delta}}+\ell_{a,\Delta})=\bar{\lambda}_{a,\Delta}\,.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>RGO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.300em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>RGO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.300em">,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>impl</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.300em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>evt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.300em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}&amp;K_{\rm RGO}\beta\eta\,\bigl\{\sqrt{d\log(1/a)}+\log(1/a)\bigr\}\leq K_{\rm RGO}c\leq 1\,,\\
&amp;\bar{\lambda}_{\rm impl}=K\beta\eta\,(\sqrt{d\ell}+\ell)\geq K_{\rm evt}\beta\eta\,(\sqrt{d\ell_{a,\Delta}}+\ell_{a,\Delta})=\bar{\lambda}_{a,\Delta}\,.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Restricted Gaussian oracle guarantee). ‣ 4.1 Implementing the restricted Gaussian oracle ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> applies with <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=a</annotation></semantics></math>, while
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2 (Capped-rate approximation and query cost). ‣ 4.2 Simulating the half-turn process ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> and monotonicity in the cap apply along every
ideal transition. If
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k}^{\rm RGO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>RGO</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}^{\rm RGO}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k}^{\rm cap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>cap</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}^{\rm cap}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the mismatch
probabilities in the corresponding couplings, then</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k}^{\rm RGO}\leq a\,,\hskip 20.00003ptp_{k}^{\rm cap}\leq a\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathbb{E}N_{\nabla V}^{\rm RGO}\leq K_{\rm RGO}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt0\leq k&lt;T\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>RGO</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>cap</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mi>RGO</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>RGO</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}^{\rm RGO}\leq a\,,\hskip 20.00003ptp_{k}^{\rm cap}\leq a\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathbb{E}N_{\nabla V}^{\rm RGO}\leq K_{\rm RGO}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt0\leq k&lt;T\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the proximal solver, let <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> minimize <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>. Under
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, write
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=X+\sqrt{\eta}Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=X+\sqrt{\eta}Z</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\mu</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\perp Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\perp Z</annotation></semantics></math>, and set</span></p>
<table id="S4.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(X,Y)\coloneqq\frac{\|(2X-Y)-\eta\nabla V(X)-X\|}{\sqrt{d\eta}}=\frac{\|\sqrt{\eta}Z+\eta\nabla V(X)\|}{\sqrt{d\eta}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(X,Y)\coloneqq\frac{\|(2X-Y)-\eta\nabla V(X)-X\|}{\sqrt{d\eta}}=\frac{\|\sqrt{\eta}Z+\eta\nabla V(X)\|}{\sqrt{d\eta}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Integration by parts gives
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\,\mathbb{E}\|X-x_{\star}\|^{2}\leq\mathbb{E}\langle\nabla V(X),X-x_{\star}\rangle=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\,\mathbb{E}\|X-x_{\star}\|^{2}\leq\mathbb{E}\langle\nabla V(X),X-x_{\star}\rangle=d</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla V(X)\|\leq\beta\,\|X-x_{\star}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla V(X)\|\leq\beta\,\|X-x_{\star}\|</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, (<a href="#A4.E7" title="Equation D.7 ‣ D.2 Strong log-concavity and covariance bounds ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.7</span></a>), and the Gaussian
norm tail, we obtain for <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S4.E16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E16X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{\pi_{\eta}}\bigl\{R(X,Y)&gt;2\sqrt{\kappa}\,\bigl(1+\sqrt{2u/d}\bigr)\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{\pi_{\eta}}\bigl\{R(X,Y)&gt;2\sqrt{\kappa}\,\bigl(1+\sqrt{2u/d}\bigr)\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(4.16)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E16Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}\bigl\{\|X-x_{\star}\|&gt;\sqrt{d/\alpha}+\sqrt{2u/\alpha}\bigr\}+\mathbb{P}\bigl\{\|Z\|&gt;\sqrt{d}+\sqrt{2u}\bigr\}\leq 2e^{-u}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">&gt;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">&gt;</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}\bigl\{\|X-x_{\star}\|&gt;\sqrt{d/\alpha}+\sqrt{2u/\alpha}\bigr\}+\mathbb{P}\bigl\{\|Z\|&gt;\sqrt{d}+\sqrt{2u}\bigr\}\leq 2e^{-u}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}\coloneqq\Delta+2\log(1/a)+\log 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}\coloneqq\Delta+2\log(1/a)+\log 2</annotation></semantics></math>. After increasing <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>,
(<a href="#S4.E14" title="Equation 4.14 ‣ Proof. ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.14</span></a>) and the definition of
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\rm prox}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\rm prox}</annotation></semantics></math> give</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}\leq C\ell\,,\hskip 20.00003ptQ_{\rm prox}\geq K_{\rm prox}\,\bigl[1+\log\bigl\{1+2\sqrt{\kappa}\,\bigl(1+\sqrt{2u_{0}/d}\bigr)\bigr\}\bigr]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}\leq C\ell\,,\hskip 20.00003ptQ_{\rm prox}\geq K_{\rm prox}\,\bigl[1+\log\bigl\{1+2\sqrt{\kappa}\,\bigl(1+\sqrt{2u_{0}/d}\bigr)\bigr\}\bigr]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is the solver failure event, then
(<a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4.4 ‣ 4.1 Implementing the restricted Gaussian oracle ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>) and
(<a href="#S4.E16" title="Equation 4.16 ‣ Proof. ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.16</span></a>) give, under stationarity,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}(\mathcal{F})\leq 2e^{-u_{0}}=e^{-\Delta}a^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}(\mathcal{F})\leq 2e^{-u_{0}}=e^{-\Delta}a^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">Cauchy–Schwarz then yields</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nu_{k}^{+}(\mathcal{F})\leq e^{D_{2}(\nu_{k}^{+}\|\pi_{\eta})/2}\,\pi_{\eta}(\mathcal{F})^{1/2}\leq a\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{k}^{+}(\mathcal{F})\leq e^{D_{2}(\nu_{k}^{+}\|\pi_{\eta})/2}\,\pi_{\eta}(\mathcal{F})^{1/2}\leq a\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Construct the preceding couplings along the ideal trajectory, using the
same Bernoulli branch variables in both chains. If <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{T}^{\rm id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>id</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{T}^{\rm id}</annotation></semantics></math>
is the ideal output, a union bound gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\{\widehat{X}\neq X_{T}^{\rm id}\}\leq\sum_{k=0}^{T-1}\bigl\{\nu_{k}^{+}(\mathcal{F})+p_{k}^{\rm RGO}+p_{k}^{\rm cap}\bigr\}\leq 3Ta=\frac{\varepsilon}{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>id</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>RGO</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>cap</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\{\widehat{X}\neq X_{T}^{\rm id}\}\leq\sum_{k=0}^{T-1}\bigl\{\nu_{k}^{+}(\mathcal{F})+p_{k}^{\rm RGO}+p_{k}^{\rm cap}\bigr\}\leq 3Ta=\frac{\varepsilon}{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{TV}\bigl(\mathcal{L}(\widehat{X}),\mu\bigr)\leq\mathbb{P}\{\widehat{X}\neq X_{T}^{\rm id}\}+\operatorname{TV}\bigl(\mathcal{L}(X_{T}^{\rm id}),\mu\bigr)\leq\varepsilon\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>id</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>TV</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>id</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{TV}\bigl(\mathcal{L}(\widehat{X}),\mu\bigr)\leq\mathbb{P}\{\widehat{X}\neq X_{T}^{\rm id}\}+\operatorname{TV}\bigl(\mathcal{L}(X_{T}^{\rm id}),\mu\bigr)\leq\varepsilon\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">which proves (<a href="#S4.E11" title="Equation 4.11 ‣ Theorem 4.3 (Sampler from an order-2 Rényi warm start). ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the query count, early termination can only help, and a half-turn
call uses one reference gradient query and an expected
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\bar{\lambda}_{\rm impl}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>impl</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\bar{\lambda}_{\rm impl}</annotation></semantics></math> queries at candidate times. Therefore</span></p>
<table id="S4.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}N_{\nabla V}\leq T\,\bigl[Q_{\rm prox}+K_{\rm RGO}+(1-\rho)\,(1+\pi\bar{\lambda}_{\rm impl})\bigr]\leq KT\,\bigl[Q_{\rm prox}+\beta\eta\,(\sqrt{d\ell}+\ell)\bigr]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>RGO</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>impl</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}N_{\nabla V}\leq T\,\bigl[Q_{\rm prox}+K_{\rm RGO}+(1-\rho)\,(1+\pi\bar{\lambda}_{\rm impl})\bigr]\leq KT\,\bigl[Q_{\rm prox}+\beta\eta\,(\sqrt{d\ell}+\ell)\bigr]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">The last inequality uses <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\rm prox}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\rm prox}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining it with
(<a href="#S4.E13" title="Equation 4.13 ‣ Proof. ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.13</span></a>) proves
(<a href="#S4.E12" title="Equation 4.12 ‣ Theorem 4.3 (Sampler from an order-2 Rényi warm start). ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.12</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 4.4</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Optimized gradient complexity)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist universal constants <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\rm opt}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\rm opt}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\rm opt}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\rm opt}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> such that the following holds. Suppose that
(<a href="#S1.E1" title="Equation 1.1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) holds, fix <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,1/4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,1/4)</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be a probability measure
on <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{2}(\mu_{0}\|\mu)\leq\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{2}(\mu_{0}\|\mu)\leq\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Set</span></p>
<table id="S4.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\coloneqq\Delta+\log\frac{K_{\rm opt}d\kappa}{\varepsilon}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\eta\coloneqq\frac{c_{\rm opt}}{\beta\,(\sqrt{dL}+L)}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\coloneqq\Delta+\log\frac{K_{\rm opt}d\kappa}{\varepsilon}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\eta\coloneqq\frac{c_{\rm opt}}{\beta\,(\sqrt{dL}+L)}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and run <a href="#alg2a" title="In 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> from <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}\sim\mu_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}\sim\mu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> using
(<a href="#S4.E8" title="Equation 4.8 ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a>)–(<a href="#S4.E9" title="Equation 4.9 ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.9</span></a>). Its output <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{X}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{TV}\bigl(\mathcal{L}(\widehat{X}),\mu\bigr)\leq\varepsilon\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{TV}\bigl(\mathcal{L}(\widehat{X}),\mu\bigr)\leq\varepsilon\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, if <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\nabla V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\nabla V}</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of gradient queries,
then</span></p>
<table id="S4.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}N_{\nabla V}\leq K_{\rm opt}\sqrt{\kappa}\,(d+L)^{1/4}\,L^{3/4}\,\Bigl(\Delta+\log\frac{4}{\varepsilon}\Bigr)\log(\kappa L)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}N_{\nabla V}\leq K_{\rm opt}\sqrt{\kappa}\,(d+L)^{1/4}\,L^{3/4}\,\Bigl(\Delta+\log\frac{4}{\varepsilon}\Bigr)\log(\kappa L)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, when <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the expected gradient
complexity is <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}(\sqrt{\kappa}\,d^{1/4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}(\sqrt{\kappa}\,d^{1/4})</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}</annotation></semantics></math> suppresses logarithmic factors in
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first verify that the tuned step size satisfies the hypotheses of
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3 (Sampler from an order-2 Rényi warm start). ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, and then simplify its query bound. Since
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the choice in
(<a href="#S4.E19" title="Equation 4.19 ‣ Corollary 4.4 (Optimized gradient complexity). ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.19</span></a>) satisfies <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leq 1/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leq 1/\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\eta=\frac{c_{\rm opt}}{\kappa\,(\sqrt{dL}+L)}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\eta=\frac{c_{\rm opt}}{\kappa\,(\sqrt{dL}+L)}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">The definitions of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> therefore imply, with
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\rm opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\rm opt}</annotation></semantics></math> large enough, that</span></p>
<table id="S4.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}\leq K_{\rm opt}L\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\ell\leq K_{\rm opt}L\,,\hskip 20.00003ptQ_{\rm prox}\leq K_{\rm opt}\log(\kappa L)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}\leq K_{\rm opt}L\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\ell\leq K_{\rm opt}L\,,\hskip 20.00003ptQ_{\rm prox}\leq K_{\rm opt}\log(\kappa L)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">The bound on <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> and the formula for <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> give</span></p>
<table id="S4.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\,(\sqrt{d\ell}+\ell)\leq\frac{K_{\rm opt}c_{\rm opt}}{\sqrt{dL}+L}\,(\sqrt{dL}+L)=K_{\rm opt}c_{\rm opt}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\,(\sqrt{d\ell}+\ell)\leq\frac{K_{\rm opt}c_{\rm opt}}{\sqrt{dL}+L}\,(\sqrt{dL}+L)=K_{\rm opt}c_{\rm opt}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Choosing <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\rm opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\rm opt}</annotation></semantics></math> small enough makes the last expression no larger
than the constant <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3 (Sampler from an order-2 Rényi warm start). ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>. This verifies
(<a href="#S4.E10" title="Equation 4.10 ‣ Theorem 4.3 (Sampler from an order-2 Rényi warm start). ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a>), so the total variation conclusion
follows from <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3 (Sampler from an order-2 Rényi warm start). ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to simplify the query bound. The choice of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}=\sqrt{\frac{\kappa}{c_{\rm opt}}}\,(\sqrt{dL}+L)^{1/2}\leq C\sqrt{\kappa}\,(dL+L^{2})^{1/4}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}=\sqrt{\frac{\kappa}{c_{\rm opt}}}\,(\sqrt{dL}+L)^{1/2}\leq C\sqrt{\kappa}\,(dL+L^{2})^{1/4}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Combining this estimate with the first inequality in
(<a href="#S4.E21" title="Equation 4.21 ‣ Proof. ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.21</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}\sqrt{\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\leq C\sqrt{\kappa}\,(dL+L^{2})^{1/4}\sqrt{L}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>L</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}\sqrt{\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\leq C\sqrt{\kappa}\,(dL+L^{2})^{1/4}\sqrt{L}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">The remaining bracket in (<a href="#S4.E12" title="Equation 4.12 ‣ Theorem 4.3 (Sampler from an order-2 Rényi warm start). ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.12</span></a>) is, by
(<a href="#S4.E21" title="Equation 4.21 ‣ Proof. ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.21</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E22" title="Equation 4.22 ‣ Proof. ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.22</span></a>), bounded by
a universal multiple of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(\kappa L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(\kappa L)</annotation></semantics></math>. Substitution into
(<a href="#S4.E12" title="Equation 4.12 ‣ Theorem 4.3 (Sampler from an order-2 Rényi warm start). ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.12</span></a>), with
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\rm opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\rm opt}</annotation></semantics></math> large enough, proves (<a href="#S4.E20" title="Equation 4.20 ‣ Corollary 4.4 (Optimized gradient complexity). ‣ Choice of parameters. ‣ 4.3 Implementable Proximal BPS and total complexity ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.20</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first construct the half-turn process up to an arbitrary time <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> at fixed <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y,\widetilde{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y,\widetilde{x})</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.
We use an integrated hazard construction <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, Section 2]</cite>
and prove reversibility by a path reversal argument. We then average over the initial momentum and
reference point in <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 The averaged ideal half-turn kernel ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> to obtain the ideal
half-turn kernel and its augmented-space lift. Finally,
<a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Bounce complexity and capped-rate implementation ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> treats the bounce count at stationarity, the
tail behaviour of the event rates, and the implementation via a capped rate.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>The fixed-reference phase space process</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of the well-posedness assertion in
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 3.1 (Well-posedness and stationarity of the conditional phase space process). ‣ 3.2 The ideal conditional half-turn process ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y,\widetilde{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y,\widetilde{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the notation of
(<a href="#S3.E4" title="Equation 3.4 ‣ 3.2 The ideal conditional half-turn process ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>), the bounce rate
(<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 3.9In Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.2 The ideal conditional half-turn process ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a>) reads</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(x,p)=\sqrt{\eta}\,[p^{\top}h_{\widetilde{x}}(x)]_{+}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(x,p)=\sqrt{\eta}\,[p^{\top}h_{\widetilde{x}}(x)]_{+}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">The deterministic harmonic flow, namely the solution
(<a href="#S4.E5" title="Equation 4.5 ‣ 4.2 Simulating the half-turn process ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>) of (<a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 3.8In Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.2 The ideal conditional half-turn process ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.8</span></a>), and
the bounce map are</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Phi_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}(x,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Phi_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}(x,p)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\bigl(c_{y,\widetilde{x}}+(x-c_{y,\widetilde{x}})\cos t+\sqrt{\eta}\,p\sin t,\;-\eta^{-1/2}(x-c_{y,\widetilde{x}})\sin t+p\cos t\bigr)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mi>p</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.028em">,</mo><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.150em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\bigl(c_{y,\widetilde{x}}+(x-c_{y,\widetilde{x}})\cos t+\sqrt{\eta}\,p\sin t,\;-\eta^{-1/2}(x-c_{y,\widetilde{x}})\sin t+p\cos t\bigr)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}(x,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}(x,p)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq(x,R_{h_{\widetilde{x}}(x)}p)\,,\hskip 20.00003ptR_{0}\coloneqq I\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.800em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq(x,R_{h_{\widetilde{x}}(x)}p)\,,\hskip 20.00003ptR_{0}\coloneqq I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">The bounce map is an involution. Although there is a possible discontinuity at <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\widetilde{x}}(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\widetilde{x}}(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, this creates no ambiguity
because the event rate vanishes there.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E_{n})_{n\geq 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E_{n})_{n\geq 1}</annotation></semantics></math> be independent <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Exp}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Exp}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>
random variables. Starting from
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{0}\coloneqq(x_{0},p_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{0}\coloneqq(x_{0},p_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}\coloneqq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}\coloneqq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, define recursively</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\inf\Bigl\{u\geq 0:\int_{0}^{u}\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\Phi_{s}^{y,\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{T_{n}}))\,\mathrm{d}s\geq E_{n+1}\Bigr\}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\inf\Bigl\{u\geq 0:\int_{0}^{u}\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\Phi_{s}^{y,\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{T_{n}}))\,\mathrm{d}s\geq E_{n+1}\Bigr\}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq T_{n}+S_{n+1}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\zeta_{T_{n+1}}\coloneqq\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}\bigl(\Phi_{S_{n+1}}^{y,\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{T_{n}})\bigr)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.150em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq T_{n}+S_{n+1}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\zeta_{T_{n+1}}\coloneqq\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}\bigl(\Phi_{S_{n+1}}^{y,\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{T_{n}})\bigr)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">when <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n+1}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n+1}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. If the set is empty, set
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{n+1}=S_{n+1}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{n+1}=S_{n+1}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and stop the recursion. Between jumps, set
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{T_{n}+t}=\Phi_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{T_{n}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{T_{n}+t}=\Phi_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{T_{n}})</annotation></semantics></math> for
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq t&lt;S_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq t&lt;S_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove non-explosion, define the shifted harmonic energy</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{y,\widetilde{x}}(x,p)\coloneqq\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl\{\eta^{-1}\,\|x-c_{y,\widetilde{x}}\|^{2}+\|p\|^{2}\bigr\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{y,\widetilde{x}}(x,p)\coloneqq\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl\{\eta^{-1}\,\|x-c_{y,\widetilde{x}}\|^{2}+\|p\|^{2}\bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">The flow and each bounce preserve this energy. Hence, with
<math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}\coloneqq H_{y,\widetilde{x}}(x_{0},p_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}\coloneqq H_{y,\widetilde{x}}(x_{0},p_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, every state produced by
the recursion satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|p\|\leq\sqrt{2\mathcal{E}}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\|x-c_{y,\widetilde{x}}\|\leq\sqrt{2\eta\mathcal{E}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|p\|\leq\sqrt{2\mathcal{E}}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\|x-c_{y,\widetilde{x}}\|\leq\sqrt{2\eta\mathcal{E}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz,
<math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(x,p)\leq\bar{\lambda}_{\mathcal{E}}(y,\widetilde{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(x,p)\leq\bar{\lambda}_{\mathcal{E}}(y,\widetilde{x})</annotation></semantics></math> throughout the path, where</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\lambda}_{\mathcal{E}}(y,\widetilde{x})\coloneqq\sqrt{\eta}\,\beta\sqrt{2\mathcal{E}}\,\bigl\{\sqrt{2\eta\mathcal{E}}+\|c_{y,\widetilde{x}}-\widetilde{x}\|\bigr\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\lambda}_{\mathcal{E}}(y,\widetilde{x})\coloneqq\sqrt{\eta}\,\beta\sqrt{2\mathcal{E}}\,\bigl\{\sqrt{2\eta\mathcal{E}}+\|c_{y,\widetilde{x}}-\widetilde{x}\|\bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{u}\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\Phi_{s}^{y,\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{T_{n}}))\,\mathrm{d}s\leq\bar{\lambda}_{\mathcal{E}}(y,\widetilde{x})\,u\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{u}\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\Phi_{s}^{y,\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{T_{n}}))\,\mathrm{d}s\leq\bar{\lambda}_{\mathcal{E}}(y,\widetilde{x})\,u\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\lambda}_{\mathcal{E}}(y,\widetilde{x})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\lambda}_{\mathcal{E}}(y,\widetilde{x})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the event rate
vanishes and there are no jumps. Otherwise,
(<a href="#A1.E1" title="Equation A.1 ‣ Proof of the well-posedness assertion in . ‣ A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>) implies, for every finite waiting time,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n+1}\geq\frac{E_{n+1}}{\bar{\lambda}_{\mathcal{E}}(y,\widetilde{x})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n+1}\geq\frac{E_{n+1}}{\bar{\lambda}_{\mathcal{E}}(y,\widetilde{x})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">If the recursion does not terminate, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{n}\geq\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{n}E_{j}}{\bar{\lambda}_{\mathcal{E}}(y,\widetilde{x})}\longrightarrow\infty" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{n}\geq\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{n}E_{j}}{\bar{\lambda}_{\mathcal{E}}(y,\widetilde{x})}\longrightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">almost surely by the strong law of large numbers. Thus, the jump times
cannot accumulate, and the recursive construction defines a unique
process for all <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, the
memoryless property of the exponential clocks gives the time-homogeneous
Markov property. This is precisely the integrated hazard construction
of Davis <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, Section 2]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">With the process now constructed, we prove the stationarity assertion in
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 3.1 (Well-posedness and stationarity of the conditional phase space process). ‣ 3.2 The ideal conditional half-turn process ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and record the stronger operator facts used
to analyze the averaged kernel. Recall <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math> from
(<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 3.1 ‣ 3.2 The ideal conditional half-turn process ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>), and define momentum
reversal by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}(x,p)\coloneqq(x,-p)\,,\hskip 20.00003pt(\mathsf{R}F)(x,p)\coloneqq F(\mathsf{R}(x,p))\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}(x,p)\coloneqq(x,-p)\,,\hskip 20.00003pt(\mathsf{R}F)(x,p)\coloneqq F(\mathsf{R}(x,p))\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">As usual, we use the same symbol for <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math> and its Lebesgue
density:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\eta,y}(x,p)\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V_{y}(x)-\frac{\|p\|^{2}}{2}\Bigr\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\eta,y}(x,p)\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V_{y}(x)-\frac{\|p\|^{2}}{2}\Bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Path reversal, invariance, and the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> semigroup)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the Markov transition
operators of the process constructed in
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 3.1 (Well-posedness and stationarity of the conditional phase space process). ‣ 3.2 The ideal conditional half-turn process ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>. For every <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}})^{*}=\mathsf{R}\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{R}\hskip 10.00002pt\text{on }L^{2}(\nu_{\eta,y})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖱𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖱</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">on </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}})^{*}=\mathsf{R}\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{R}\hskip 10.00002pt\text{on }L^{2}(\nu_{\eta,y})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2.2em;">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is invariant;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a strongly continuous
contraction semigroup on </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\nu_{\eta,y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\nu_{\eta,y})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">if </span><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}:L^{2}(\nu_{\eta,y})\to L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}:L^{2}(\nu_{\eta,y})\to L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> denotes Gaussian momentum averaging, then
</span><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a
self-adjoint Markov contraction on </span><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Idea of the proof.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The identity (<a href="#A1.E3" title="Equation A.3 ‣ Proposition A.1 (Path reversal, invariance, and the 𝐿^2 semigroup). ‣ A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>) is a
momentum-reversed form of detailed balance. To see the mechanism
formally, write
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{x}}=\mathcal{A}+\mathcal{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{x}}=\mathcal{A}+\mathcal{J}</annotation></semantics></math>, where</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{A}f(x,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{A}f(x,p)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\sqrt{\eta}\,p^{\top}\nabla_{x}f(x,p)-\frac{(x-c_{y,\widetilde{x}})^{\top}}{\sqrt{\eta}}\nabla_{p}f(x,p)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\sqrt{\eta}\,p^{\top}\nabla_{x}f(x,p)-\frac{(x-c_{y,\widetilde{x}})^{\top}}{\sqrt{\eta}}\nabla_{p}f(x,p),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{J}f(x,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{J}f(x,p)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(x,p)\bigl\{f(\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}(x,p))-f(x,p)\bigr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(x,p)\bigl\{f(\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}(x,p))-f(x,p)\bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Momentum reversal reverses the harmonic flow, so
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}\mathcal{A}\mathsf{R}=-\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖱</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}\mathcal{A}\mathsf{R}=-\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}\log\nu_{\eta,y}(x,p)=-\sqrt{\eta}\,p^{\top}h_{\widetilde{x}}(x)=-\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(x,p)+\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(x,-p)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\log\nu_{\eta,y}(x,p)=-\sqrt{\eta}\,p^{\top}h_{\widetilde{x}}(x)=-\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(x,p)+\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(x,-p).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Formal integration by parts gives</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{*}=-\mathcal{A}+\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}-\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}\circ\mathsf{R}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝖱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{*}=-\mathcal{A}+\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}-\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}\circ\mathsf{R}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The bounce map <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>-preserving involution, commutes with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
satisfies <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}\circ\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}=\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}\circ\mathsf{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝖱</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}\circ\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}=\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}\circ\mathsf{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. A formal change of variables
therefore gives</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}^{*}G=(\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}\circ\mathsf{R})(G\circ\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}})-\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}G." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝖱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}^{*}G=(\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}\circ\mathsf{R})(G\circ\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}})-\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}G.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Combining the two identities yields</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{x}}^{*}G=-\mathcal{A}G+(\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}\circ\mathsf{R})(G\circ\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}-G)=(\mathsf{R}\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{R})G." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖫</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝖱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱𝖫</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{x}}^{*}G=-\mathcal{A}G+(\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}\circ\mathsf{R})(G\circ\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}-G)=(\mathsf{R}\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{R})G.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Formally exponentiating this identity gives
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}})^{*}=\mathsf{R}\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖱𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖱</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}})^{*}=\mathsf{R}\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{R}</annotation></semantics></math>; Gaussian momentum averaging
then removes <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and produces an ordinary self-adjoint position
kernel.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This generator calculation is only heuristic as stated, as the standard arguments are not
immediately applicable because
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> may be discontinuous where
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\widetilde{x}}(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\widetilde{x}}(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. The pathwise argument below proves the same
identity without requiring differentiability or continuity of the
bounce map.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Along
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{s}=(x_{s},p_{s})=\Phi_{s}^{y,\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{s}=(x_{s},p_{s})=\Phi_{s}^{y,\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}s}\log\nu_{\eta,y}(\zeta_{s})=-\sqrt{\eta}\,p_{s}^{\top}h_{\widetilde{x}}(x_{s})=-\bigl\{\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{s})-\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\mathsf{R}\zeta_{s})\bigr\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}s}\log\nu_{\eta,y}(\zeta_{s})=-\sqrt{\eta}\,p_{s}^{\top}h_{\widetilde{x}}(x_{s})=-\bigl\{\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{s})-\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\mathsf{R}\zeta_{s})\bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, by definition of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}\Phi_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{R}=\Phi_{-t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{R}\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}=\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{R}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖱</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱𝖲</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}\Phi_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{R}=\Phi_{-t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{R}\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}=\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{R}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta^{+}=\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}\zeta^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ζ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ζ</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta^{+}=\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}\zeta^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> is a non-trivial jump, then
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\widetilde{x}}(x)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\widetilde{x}}(x)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p^{-})^{\top}h_{\widetilde{x}}(x)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p^{-})^{\top}h_{\widetilde{x}}(x)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\zeta^{-})=\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\mathsf{R}\zeta^{+})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ζ</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ζ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\zeta^{-})=\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\mathsf{R}\zeta^{+})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">The flow and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}</annotation></semantics></math> preserve Lebesgue measure, as does the possibly
discontinuous bounce map: by Fubini’s theorem and orthogonality, for
every integrable <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int F(\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}(x,p))\,\mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}p=\int F(x,p)\,\mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}p\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int F(\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}(x,p))\,\mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}p=\int F(x,p)\,\mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}p\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">To pass from these identities to complete trajectories, let</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{n}(t)\coloneqq\{(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n}):0&lt;t_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;t_{n}&lt;t\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{n}(t)\coloneqq\{(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n}):0&lt;t_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;t_{n}&lt;t\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Given <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{t}\in\Delta_{n}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{t}\in\Delta_{n}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, let
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{s}^{\zeta_{0},\mathbf{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐭</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{s}^{\zeta_{0},\mathbf{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the path obtained by following
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{y,\widetilde{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{y,\widetilde{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and applying <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> at the
prescribed times. Iterating the exponential clock construction gives,
for every bounded measurable functional <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> of the path up to time
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\zeta_{0}}\Psi(\zeta_{[0,t]})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\zeta_{0}}\Psi(\zeta_{[0,t]})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\int_{\Delta_{n}(t)}\Psi(\zeta_{[0,t]}^{\zeta_{0},\mathbf{t}})\exp\Bigl\{-\!\int_{0}^{t}\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{s}^{\zeta_{0},\mathbf{t}})\,\mathrm{d}s\Bigr\}\prod_{j=1}^{n}\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{t_{j}-}^{\zeta_{0},\mathbf{t}})\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{t}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐭</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐭</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐭</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐭</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\int_{\Delta_{n}(t)}\Psi(\zeta_{[0,t]}^{\zeta_{0},\mathbf{t}})\exp\Bigl\{-\!\int_{0}^{t}\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{s}^{\zeta_{0},\mathbf{t}})\,\mathrm{d}s\Bigr\}\prod_{j=1}^{n}\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{t_{j}-}^{\zeta_{0},\mathbf{t}})\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{t}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">The series is absolutely convergent because
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert\Delta_{n}(t)\rvert=t^{n}/n!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert\Delta_{n}(t)\rvert=t^{n}/n!</annotation></semantics></math> and the rate
is bounded by <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\lambda}_{\mathcal{E}}(y,\widetilde{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\lambda}_{\mathcal{E}}(y,\widetilde{x})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Integrate (<a href="#A1.E7" title="Equation A.7 ‣ Proof. ‣ Idea of the proof. ‣ A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>) against
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\eta,y}(\mathrm{d}\zeta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\eta,y}(\mathrm{d}\zeta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and apply</span></p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\zeta_{s})_{0\leq s\leq t}\longmapsto(\mathsf{R}\zeta_{t-s})_{0\leq s\leq t}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n})\longmapsto(t-t_{n},\ldots,t-t_{1})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟼</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\zeta_{s})_{0\leq s\leq t}\longmapsto(\mathsf{R}\zeta_{t-s})_{0\leq s\leq t}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n})\longmapsto(t-t_{n},\ldots,t-t_{1})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">For completeness, we justify this change of variables despite the
possible discontinuity of the bounce map. For fixed
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{t}\in\Delta_{n}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{t}\in\Delta_{n}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, the endpoint map
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{0}\mapsto\zeta_{t}^{\zeta_{0},\mathbf{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐭</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{0}\mapsto\zeta_{t}^{\zeta_{0},\mathbf{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite composition
of the Borel involution <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{S}_{\widetilde{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the affine
harmonic flows <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{u}^{y,\widetilde{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{u}^{y,\widetilde{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By
(<a href="#A1.E6" title="Equation A.6 ‣ Proof. ‣ Idea of the proof. ‣ A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>) and the explicit flow formula, each factor is
a measure-preserving Borel bijection. Hence the endpoint map, and
therefore
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{0}\mapsto\mathsf{R}\zeta_{t}^{\zeta_{0},\mathbf{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐭</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{0}\mapsto\mathsf{R}\zeta_{t}^{\zeta_{0},\mathbf{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is a Borel
measure-preserving bijection. The identities preceding
(<a href="#A1.E7" title="Equation A.7 ‣ Proof. ‣ Idea of the proof. ‣ A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>) show that its inverse is obtained by
using the reversed ordered times in (<a href="#A1.E8" title="Equation A.8 ‣ Proof. ‣ Idea of the proof. ‣ A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>). The
map on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{n}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{n}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is linear with absolute determinant one.
Thus the full change of variables is measure preserving; no Jacobian is needed.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Integrating (<a href="#A1.E4" title="Equation A.4 ‣ Proof. ‣ Idea of the proof. ‣ A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>) over the deterministic arcs
and using that a reflection preserves <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nu_{\eta,y}(\zeta_{0})\,e^{-\int_{0}^{t}\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{s})\,\mathrm{d}s}=\nu_{\eta,y}(\zeta_{t})\,e^{-\int_{0}^{t}\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\mathsf{R}\zeta_{s})\,\mathrm{d}s}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.800em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.800em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\eta,y}(\zeta_{0})\,e^{-\int_{0}^{t}\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\zeta_{s})\,\mathrm{d}s}=\nu_{\eta,y}(\zeta_{t})\,e^{-\int_{0}^{t}\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\mathsf{R}\zeta_{s})\,\mathrm{d}s}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">This identity matches the initial density and survival factor of a
forward path with those of its reversal, while
(<a href="#A1.E5" title="Equation A.5 ‣ Proof. ‣ Idea of the proof. ‣ A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>) matches every jump-rate factor. Hence,
each <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-jump term in (<a href="#A1.E7" title="Equation A.7 ‣ Proof. ‣ Idea of the proof. ‣ A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>) is unchanged by
(<a href="#A1.E8" title="Equation A.8 ‣ Proof. ‣ Idea of the proof. ‣ A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>). Tonelli’s theorem justifies the termwise
change of variables for non-negative bounded functions; decomposing
signed functions into positive and negative parts then gives, for
bounded measurable <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F,G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F,G</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int F\,\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}G\,\mathrm{d}\nu_{\eta,y}=\int(\mathsf{R}G)\,\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}(\mathsf{R}F)\,\mathrm{d}\nu_{\eta,y}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int F\,\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}G\,\mathrm{d}\nu_{\eta,y}=\int(\mathsf{R}G)\,\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}(\mathsf{R}F)\,\mathrm{d}\nu_{\eta,y}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=1</annotation></semantics></math> proves invariance, and the identity extends by density to
(<a href="#A1.E3" title="Equation A.3 ‣ Proposition A.1 (Path reversal, invariance, and the 𝐿^2 semigroup). ‣ A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>) on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\nu_{\eta,y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\nu_{\eta,y})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Invariance and Jensen’s inequality give
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}F\|_{2}\leq\|F\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}F\|_{2}\leq\|F\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. It remains to prove
strong continuity. For <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in C_{\rm c}(\mathbb{R}^{2d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in C_{\rm c}(\mathbb{R}^{2d})</annotation></semantics></math>, the deterministic flow
converges to the identity as <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\searrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>↘</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\searrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and the probability of a jump before time
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1-\exp\Bigl\{-\int_{0}^{t}\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\Phi_{s}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\zeta)\,\mathrm{d}s\Bigr\}\longrightarrow 0\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>λ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\exp\Bigl\{-\int_{0}^{t}\lambda_{\widetilde{x}}(\Phi_{s}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\zeta)\,\mathrm{d}s\Bigr\}\longrightarrow 0\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Dominated convergence therefore gives
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}F\to F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}F\to F</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Density of
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\rm c}(\mathbb{R}^{2d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\rm c}(\mathbb{R}^{2d})</annotation></semantics></math> and contractivity extend this to all <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, Gaussian momentum averaging satisfies
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*}=\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*}=\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}\mathsf{R}=\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖱</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}\mathsf{R}=\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining these identities with
(<a href="#A1.E3" title="Equation A.3 ‣ Proposition A.1 (Path reversal, invariance, and the 𝐿^2 semigroup). ‣ A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*})^{*}=\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}(\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}})^{*}\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*}=\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}\mathsf{R}\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{R}\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*}=\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖱𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*})^{*}=\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}(\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}})^{*}\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*}=\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}\mathsf{R}\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{R}\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*}=\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">This proves self-adjointness; the Markov and contraction properties are
inherited from <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>The averaged ideal half-turn kernel</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 3.2 (Reversibility of the conditional half-turn kernel). ‣ 3.2 The ideal conditional half-turn process ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. For each reference point <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition A.1 (Path reversal, invariance, and the 𝐿^2 semigroup). ‣ A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> shows that the fixed-reference
position operator
<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}\mathsf{T}_{\pi}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}\mathsf{T}_{\pi}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is a self-adjoint
Markov contraction on <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y})</annotation></semantics></math>. The reference
point in <a href="#alg1" title="In 3.2 The ideal conditional half-turn process ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is drawn independently from
<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, the conditional half-turn
operator is the average</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{H}_{y}f)(x)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\bigl(\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}\mathsf{T}_{\pi}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*}f\bigr)(x)\,\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}(\mathrm{d}\widetilde{x})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Π</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{H}_{y}f)(x)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\bigl(\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}\mathsf{T}_{\pi}^{y,\widetilde{x}}\mathsf{\Pi}_{p}^{*}f\bigr)(x)\,\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}(\mathrm{d}\widetilde{x})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">The averaging measure does not depend on <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is again a
self-adjoint Markov contraction. In kernel form, this is the
detailed-balance identity</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}(\mathrm{d}x)\,\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})=\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}(\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})\,\mathcal{H}_{y}(x^{\prime},\mathrm{d}x)\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}(\mathrm{d}x)\,\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})=\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}(\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})\,\mathcal{H}_{y}(x^{\prime},\mathrm{d}x)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">which proves the proposition.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The preceding reversibility statement holds for each fixed <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. To use
these kernels as a single operator on the augmented space, we next verify
their joint measurability and then integrate the conditional operator
identities over <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Joint measurability and augmented space half-turn operator)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The family of conditional half-turn kernels
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{H}_{y})_{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{H}_{y})_{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a version, again denoted by
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, such that
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y,x)\mapsto\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y,x)\mapsto\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,A)</annotation></semantics></math> is Borel measurable for every
Borel set <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{H}f)(x,y)\coloneqq\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x^{\prime},y)\,\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖧</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{H}f)(x,y)\coloneqq\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(x^{\prime},y)\,\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">defines a self-adjoint Markov contraction on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous, the harmonic flow, event rate, and
reflection map are jointly Borel; the convention <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}=I</annotation></semantics></math> ensures
this even where the reflection normal vanishes. The integrated hazard
is jointly Borel, with continuous, nondecreasing dependence on time, so its
threshold-crossing times are Borel, as can be checked using rational
times. Thus the recursion
(<a href="#A1.E1" title="Equation A.1 ‣ Proof of the well-posedness assertion in . ‣ A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>)–(<a href="#A1.E2" title="Equation A.2 ‣ Proof of the well-posedness assertion in . ‣ A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>)
makes each jump time and post-jump state Borel in
<math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y,x_{0},p_{0},\widetilde{x},(E_{j})_{j\geq 1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y,x_{0},p_{0},\widetilde{x},(E_{j})_{j\geq 1})</annotation></semantics></math>.
By non-explosion, the terminal state at time <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is the almost-sure
limit of the Borel terminal states obtained by allowing at most <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>
jumps. Setting the limit to zero wherever it does not exist gives a
Borel version.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The conditional density in (<a href="#S2.E8" title="Equation 2.8 ‣ 2.2 Proximal augmentation and the restricted Gaussian oracle ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.8</span></a>) is jointly
Borel in <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y,\widetilde{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y,\widetilde{x})</annotation></semantics></math>. Integrating <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{\{x_{\pi}\in A\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.280em" minsize="1.280em">{</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo maxsize="1.280em" minsize="1.280em">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{\{x_{\pi}\in A\}}</annotation></semantics></math>
against this reference law and the laws of the Gaussian momentum and
exponential clocks therefore makes <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y,x)\mapsto\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y,x)\mapsto\mathcal{H}_{y}(x,A)</annotation></semantics></math>
Borel for every Borel set <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, each <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is a self-adjoint Markov contraction by
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 3.2 (Reversibility of the conditional half-turn kernel). ‣ 3.2 The ideal conditional half-turn process ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>. Integrating the conditional contraction
bound gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathsf{H}f\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖧</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathsf{H}f\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\int\bigl\|f(\cdot,y)\bigr\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y})}^{2}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)=\|f\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})}^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\int\bigl\|f(\cdot,y)\bigr\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y})}^{2}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)=\|f\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Conditional self-adjointness and Fubini likewise give
<math id="A1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle f,\mathsf{H}g\rangle=\langle\mathsf{H}f,g\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝖧</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖧</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle f,\mathsf{H}g\rangle=\langle\mathsf{H}f,g\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> for bounded
measurable <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f,g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f,g</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence for all <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math> by density.
Positivity and <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}1=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖧</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}1=1</annotation></semantics></math> follow from the corresponding properties of
each <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Bounce complexity and capped-rate implementation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Stationary bounce count). ‣ 3.2 The ideal conditional half-turn process ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> follows immediately from the following lemma. More specifically, for every fixed
<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y,\widetilde{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y,\widetilde{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition A.1 (Path reversal, invariance, and the 𝐿^2 semigroup). ‣ A.1 The fixed-reference phase space process ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> shows that the
phase space process preserves <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, under the
initialization in the proposition and conditional on <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=y</annotation></semantics></math>, the triple
<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{t},p_{t},\widetilde{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{t},p_{t},\widetilde{X})</annotation></semantics></math> has law
<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I)\otimes\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I)\otimes\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}</annotation></semantics></math> at
every time <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,\pi]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,\pi]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Tail bound for the event rate)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,\widetilde{X}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\rm iid}}{{\sim}}\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>iid</mi></mover><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,\widetilde{X}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\rm iid}}{{\sim}}\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math> be independent, and set <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\coloneqq\sqrt{\eta}\,[P^{\top}(\nabla V(X)-\nabla V(\widetilde{X}))]_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\coloneqq\sqrt{\eta}\,[P^{\top}(\nabla V(X)-\nabla V(\widetilde{X}))]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For every <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\bigl\{\lambda&gt;C\beta\eta\,(\sqrt{du}+u)\bigr\}\leq Ce^{-u}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>β</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\bigl\{\lambda&gt;C\beta\eta\,(\sqrt{du}+u)\bigr\}\leq Ce^{-u}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently, for <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\lambda}_{\ell}=C\beta\eta\,(\sqrt{d\ell}+\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\lambda}_{\ell}=C\beta\eta\,(\sqrt{d\ell}+\ell)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(\lambda-\bar{\lambda}_{\ell})_{+}\leq C\beta\eta\sqrt{d}\,e^{-c\ell}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(\lambda-\bar{\lambda}_{\ell})_{+}\leq C\beta\eta\sqrt{d}\,e^{-c\ell}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The measure <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha+\eta^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha+\eta^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly log-concave, and therefore
(<a href="#A4.E7" title="Equation D.7 ‣ D.2 Strong log-concavity and covariance bounds ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.7</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\bigl\{\|X-\mathbb{E}X\|\geq C\sqrt{\eta\,(d+u)}\bigr\}\leq e^{-u}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≥</mo><mi>C</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\bigl\{\|X-\mathbb{E}X\|\geq C\sqrt{\eta\,(d+u)}\bigr\}\leq e^{-u}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">for every <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\bigl\{\sqrt{\eta}\,\|\nabla V(X)-\nabla V(\widetilde{X})\|&gt;2C\beta\eta\sqrt{d+u}\bigr\}\leq 2e^{-u}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>C</mi><mi>β</mi><mi>η</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\bigl\{\sqrt{\eta}\,\|\nabla V(X)-\nabla V(\widetilde{X})\|&gt;2C\beta\eta\sqrt{d+u}\bigr\}\leq 2e^{-u}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Conditional on
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=\sqrt{\eta}\,\{\nabla V(X)-\nabla V(\widetilde{X})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=\sqrt{\eta}\,\{\nabla V(X)-\nabla V(\widetilde{X})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the scalar
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\top}h\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\|h\|^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\top}h\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\|h\|^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. The Gaussian tail and a union bound
with (<a href="#A1.E12" title="Equation A.12 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.3 Bounce complexity and capped-rate implementation ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.12</span></a>) therefore show that, for <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and outside an event
of probability at most <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2e^{-u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2e^{-u}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[P^{\top}h]_{+}\leq C\sqrt{u}\,\|h\|\leq C\beta\eta\,(\sqrt{du}+u)\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>u</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[P^{\top}h]_{+}\leq C\sqrt{u}\,\|h\|\leq C\beta\eta\,(\sqrt{du}+u)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">which proves (<a href="#A1.E10" title="Equation A.10 ‣ Lemma A.3 (Tail bound for the event rate). ‣ A.3 Bounce complexity and capped-rate implementation ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.10</span></a>) in this range.
The bound for <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq u&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq u&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> follows after increasing <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> accordingly.
Finally, (<a href="#A1.E11" title="Equation A.11 ‣ Lemma A.3 (Tail bound for the event rate). ‣ A.3 Bounce complexity and capped-rate implementation ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a>) follows by integration.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2 (Capped-rate approximation and query cost). ‣ 4.2 Simulating the half-turn process ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For part (i), first suppose that <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{0},Y)\sim\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{0},Y)\sim\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and write
<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\pi_{\eta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\pi_{\eta}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\eta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\eta}}</annotation></semantics></math> for probability and
expectation under the resulting coupled construction, including the
reference point, initial momentum, and Poisson random measure shared by
the ideal and capped processes. Let <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> be the event that
the two paths separate. The paths agree until the first event from
the excess rate <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda_{t}-\bar{\lambda}_{\xi,\Delta})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda_{t}-\bar{\lambda}_{\xi,\Delta})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the
probability of <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by the expected number of
such events:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\pi_{\eta}}(\mathcal{D})\leq\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\eta}}\int_{0}^{\pi}(\lambda_{t}-\bar{\lambda}_{\xi,\Delta})_{+}\,\mathrm{d}t\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\pi_{\eta}}(\mathcal{D})\leq\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\eta}}\int_{0}^{\pi}(\lambda_{t}-\bar{\lambda}_{\xi,\Delta})_{+}\,\mathrm{d}t\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">By stationarity, (<a href="#A1.E11" title="Equation A.11 ‣ Lemma A.3 (Tail bound for the event rate). ‣ A.3 Bounce complexity and capped-rate implementation ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a>) applies at every <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the
small-scale assumption implies
<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\sqrt{d}\leq c_{\rm evt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>evt</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\sqrt{d}\leq c_{\rm evt}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\pi_{\eta}}(\mathcal{D})\leq Ce^{-c\ell_{\xi,\Delta}}\leq e^{-\Delta}\xi^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\pi_{\eta}}(\mathcal{D})\leq Ce^{-c\ell_{\xi,\Delta}}\leq e^{-\Delta}\xi^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">The definition of <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\xi,\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\xi,\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S4.E6" title="Equation 4.6 ‣ Item (i) ‣ Proposition 4.2 (Capped-rate approximation and query cost). ‣ 4.2 Simulating the half-turn process ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a>) gives
the last inequality after increasing <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\rm evt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>evt</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\rm evt}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now let <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy
<math id="A1.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{2}(\nu_{0}\|\pi_{\eta})\leq\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{2}(\nu_{0}\|\pi_{\eta})\leq\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, and set
<math id="A1.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0}=\mathrm{d}\nu_{0}/\mathrm{d}\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}=\mathrm{d}\nu_{0}/\mathrm{d}\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Relative to the coupled path law
<math id="A1.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\pi_{\eta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\pi_{\eta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the construction started from <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> has
likelihood ratio <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0}(X_{0},Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}(X_{0},Y)</annotation></semantics></math>: all reference points, momenta, and Poisson
variables are generated by the same conditional rules. Hence,
Cauchy–Schwarz gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\nu_{0}}(\mathcal{D})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\eta}}[h_{0}(X_{0},Y)\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{D}}]\leq(\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\eta}}h_{0}^{2})^{1/2}\,\mathbb{P}_{\pi_{\eta}}(\mathcal{D})^{1/2}\leq e^{\Delta/2}\,(e^{-\Delta}\xi^{2})^{1/2}=\xi\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\nu_{0}}(\mathcal{D})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\eta}}[h_{0}(X_{0},Y)\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{D}}]\leq(\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\eta}}h_{0}^{2})^{1/2}\,\mathbb{P}_{\pi_{\eta}}(\mathcal{D})^{1/2}\leq e^{\Delta/2}\,(e^{-\Delta}\xi^{2})^{1/2}=\xi\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">This proves part (i).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For part (ii), the number of arrivals of the
rate-<math id="A1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\lambda}_{\xi,\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\lambda}_{\xi,\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> proposal clock before time <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>
is Poisson with mean <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\bar{\lambda}_{\xi,\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\bar{\lambda}_{\xi,\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the
reference gradient is already cached, the capped simulation makes
exactly one gradient query at each arrival. This proves
(<a href="#S4.E7" title="Equation 4.7 ‣ Item (ii) ‣ Proposition 4.2 (Capped-rate approximation and query cost). ‣ 4.2 Simulating the half-turn process ‣ 4 Efficient implementation of Proximal BPS ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Operator formulation and modified <math id="A2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> contraction</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix proves <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 3.5 (𝜒^2 convergence). ‣ 3.3 Ideal Proximal BPS ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> using the modified <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
hypocoercivity framework of Dolbeault, Mouhot, and Schmeiser <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite> and Fan, Li, and Lu <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>. We first set
up the operator framework and then derive the contraction from two
model-specific estimates proved in Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Operator framework and micro–macro decomposition</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our target distribution is the joint law <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in
(<a href="#S2.E6" title="Equation 2.6 ‣ 2.2 Proximal augmentation and the restricted Gaussian oracle ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.6</span></a>), and we set <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}\coloneqq L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}\coloneqq L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall from
(<a href="#S3.E11" title="Equation 3.11 ‣ 3.3 Ideal Proximal BPS ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.11</span></a>) that the ideal Proximal BPS has
transition kernel</p>
<table id="A2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}\bigl((x,y),\mathrm{d}x^{\prime}\,\mathrm{d}y^{\prime}\bigr)=\delta_{2x-y}(\mathrm{d}y^{\prime})\,\bigl[\rho\,\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y^{\prime}}(\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})+(1-\rho)\,\mathcal{H}_{y^{\prime}}(x,\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})\bigr]\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.150em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}\bigl((x,y),\mathrm{d}x^{\prime}\,\mathrm{d}y^{\prime}\bigr)=\delta_{2x-y}(\mathrm{d}y^{\prime})\,\bigl[\rho\,\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y^{\prime}}(\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})+(1-\rho)\,\mathcal{H}_{y^{\prime}}(x,\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})\bigr]\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{y^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{y^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the conditional half-turn kernel from
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 3.2 (Reversibility of the conditional half-turn kernel). ‣ 3.2 The ideal conditional half-turn process ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>. Since the algorithm is a discrete-time
chain, its evolution is described by the induced one-step Markov operator
on observables,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{K}f)(x,y)\coloneqq\int_{\mathbb{R}^{2d}}f(x^{\prime},y^{\prime})\,\mathcal{K}\bigl((x,y),\mathrm{d}x^{\prime}\,\mathrm{d}y^{\prime}\bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{K}f)(x,y)\coloneqq\int_{\mathbb{R}^{2d}}f(x^{\prime},y^{\prime})\,\mathcal{K}\bigl((x,y),\mathrm{d}x^{\prime}\,\mathrm{d}y^{\prime}\bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> acts on probability laws, whereas <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is its
induced action on observables. The first term in brackets
in <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is the conditional resampling branch. After the
auxiliary coordinate is updated to <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,
this branch replaces the <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-coordinate by an independent draw from
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The associated conditional expectation operator
is</p>
<table id="A2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{P}f)(x,y)\coloneqq\int f(x^{\prime},y)\,\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}(\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})=\mathbb{E}[f(X,Y)\mid Y=y]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{P}f)(x,y)\coloneqq\int f(x^{\prime},y)\,\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}(\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})=\mathbb{E}[f(X,Y)\mid Y=y]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">In particular, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}f</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on the coordinate <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. The range
and kernel of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}</annotation></semantics></math> are</p>
<table id="A2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}&amp;\coloneqq\operatorname{ran}(\mathsf{P})=\{f\in\mathfrak{H}:f(x,y)=g(y)\text{ for some }g\in L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})\}\,,\\
\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}&amp;\coloneqq\ker(\mathsf{P})=\operatorname{ran}(\mathsf{P}^{\perp})=\{f\in\mathfrak{H}:\mathbb{E}[f(X,Y)\mid Y]=0\}\,.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>ran</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℌ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for some </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.300em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ran</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℌ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.022em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}&amp;\coloneqq\operatorname{ran}(\mathsf{P})=\{f\in\mathfrak{H}:f(x,y)=g(y)\text{ for some }g\in L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})\}\,,\\
\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}&amp;\coloneqq\ker(\mathsf{P})=\operatorname{ran}(\mathsf{P}^{\perp})=\{f\in\mathfrak{H}:\mathbb{E}[f(X,Y)\mid Y]=0\}\,.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\coloneqq I-\mathsf{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\coloneqq I-\mathsf{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}=\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\oplus\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}=\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\oplus\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=\mathsf{P}f+\mathsf{P}^{\perp}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=\mathsf{P}f+\mathsf{P}^{\perp}f</annotation></semantics></math>. In the common terminology of
hypocoercivity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{ran}(\mathsf{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ran</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{ran}(\mathsf{P})</annotation></semantics></math> is the
<em id="A2.SS1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">macroscopic</em> subspace and its orthogonal complement is the
<em id="A2.SS1.p1.5.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">microscopic</em> subspace.
Thus functions in <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> depend only on the coordinate <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>,
whereas functions in <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> have zero mean under
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{X\mid Y=y}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>-almost every <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Relative to the decomposition
<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}=\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\oplus\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}=\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\oplus\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>, we write an operator
<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℌ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}</annotation></semantics></math> in block form as</p>
<table id="A2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathsf{T}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}&amp;\mathsf{T}_{\mathsf{P}\perp}\\
\mathsf{T}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}&amp;\mathsf{T}_{\perp\perp}\end{pmatrix}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\begin{aligned} \mathsf{T}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}&amp;\coloneqq\mathsf{P}\mathsf{T}\mathsf{P}\,,&amp;\mathsf{T}_{\mathsf{P}\perp}&amp;\coloneqq\mathsf{P}\mathsf{T}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\,,\\
\mathsf{T}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}&amp;\coloneqq\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\mathsf{T}\mathsf{P}\,,&amp;\mathsf{T}_{\perp\perp}&amp;\coloneqq\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\mathsf{T}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\,.\end{aligned}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝖳</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝖳</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝖳</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mi>𝖯𝖳𝖯</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>𝖳</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><msup><mi>𝖯𝖳𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>𝖳</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖳𝖯</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>𝖳</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝖳𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathsf{T}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}&amp;\mathsf{T}_{\mathsf{P}\perp}\\
\mathsf{T}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}&amp;\mathsf{T}_{\perp\perp}\end{pmatrix}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\begin{aligned} \mathsf{T}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}&amp;\coloneqq\mathsf{P}\mathsf{T}\mathsf{P}\,,&amp;\mathsf{T}_{\mathsf{P}\perp}&amp;\coloneqq\mathsf{P}\mathsf{T}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\,,\\
\mathsf{T}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}&amp;\coloneqq\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\mathsf{T}\mathsf{P}\,,&amp;\mathsf{T}_{\perp\perp}&amp;\coloneqq\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\mathsf{T}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\,.\end{aligned}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The first subscript specifies the target subspace and the second the source
subspace; thus <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}_{ab}:\mathfrak{H}_{b}\to\mathfrak{H}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖳</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}_{ab}:\mathfrak{H}_{b}\to\mathfrak{H}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> for
<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in\{\mathsf{P},\perp\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⟂</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in\{\mathsf{P},\perp\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We first apply this block notation to the reflection map <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}</annotation></semantics></math> from
(<a href="#S2.E14" title="Equation 2.14 ‣ Item (iii) ‣ Proposition 2.1 (Geometry of the joint law). ‣ 2.2 Proximal augmentation and the restricted Gaussian oracle ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.14</span></a>). We use the same symbol for its pullback on
observables:</p>
<table id="A2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{U}f)(x,y)\coloneqq f(\mathsf{U}(x,y))=f(x,2x-y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{U}f)(x,y)\coloneqq f(\mathsf{U}(x,y))=f(x,2x-y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This pullback is self-adjoint and unitary, and hence has block matrix</p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}&amp;\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\
\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}&amp;\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}\end{pmatrix}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖴</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}&amp;\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\
\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}&amp;\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}\end{pmatrix}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{P}\mathsf{U}\mathsf{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖯𝖴𝖯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{P}\mathsf{U}\mathsf{P}</annotation></semantics></math> maps <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> to itself, whereas
<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\mathsf{U}\mathsf{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖴𝖯</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\mathsf{U}\mathsf{P}</annotation></semantics></math> maps <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since
<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}</annotation></semantics></math> is self-adjoint and unitary, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a self-adjoint
contraction on <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Writing <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}^{2}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝖴</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}^{2}=I</annotation></semantics></math> in blocks gives</p>
<table id="A2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We next express the joint half-turn operator <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖧</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}</annotation></semantics></math> in the same block
decomposition. It is defined in (<a href="#A1.E9" title="Equation A.9 ‣ Proposition A.2 (Joint measurability and augmented space half-turn operator). ‣ A.2 The averaged ideal half-turn kernel ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.9</span></a>) and is a
self-adjoint Markov contraction by
<a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition A.2 (Joint measurability and augmented space half-turn operator). ‣ A.2 The averaged ideal half-turn kernel ‣ Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>. Since <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖧</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}</annotation></semantics></math> acts only on the
<math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-coordinate, while every
function in <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{ran}(\mathsf{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ran</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{ran}(\mathsf{P})</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A2.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}\mathsf{P}=\mathsf{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖧𝖯</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}\mathsf{P}=\mathsf{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. Self-adjointness also gives
<math id="A2.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}\mathsf{H}=\mathsf{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯𝖧</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}\mathsf{H}=\mathsf{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. Set
<math id="A2.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\mathsf{H}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}:\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}\to\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝖧𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\mathsf{H}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}:\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}\to\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The identity <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}\mathsf{H}=\mathsf{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯𝖧</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}\mathsf{H}=\mathsf{P}</annotation></semantics></math> makes <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> invariant under
<math id="A2.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖧</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> is its restriction to <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is
therefore self-adjoint, and
<math id="A2.SS1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}g\|=\|\mathsf{H}g\|\leq\|g\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖧</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}g\|=\|\mathsf{H}g\|\leq\|g\|</annotation></semantics></math> for
<math id="A2.SS1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently,</p>
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{H}=\mathsf{P}+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt-I\preceq\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\preceq I\hskip 10.00002pt\text{on }\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖧</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝖧</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.778em">,</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mi>𝖧</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi><mtext>on </mtext><mi>ℌ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}=\mathsf{P}+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt-I\preceq\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\preceq I\hskip 10.00002pt\text{on }\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Relative to <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}=\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\oplus\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}=\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\oplus\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>, this decomposition
has the block representation</p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}=\begin{pmatrix}I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}}&amp;0\\
0&amp;\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\end{pmatrix}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖧</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}=\begin{pmatrix}I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}}&amp;0\\
0&amp;\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\end{pmatrix}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">The Markov operator <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}</annotation></semantics></math> induced by the transition kernel <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math>
therefore factors as</p>
<table id="A2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}=\mathsf{U}\bigl[\rho\mathsf{P}+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}\bigr]=\mathsf{U}\bigl[\mathsf{P}+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖧</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}=\mathsf{U}\bigl[\rho\mathsf{P}+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}\bigr]=\mathsf{U}\bigl[\mathsf{P}+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p">Accordingly, its block representation is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}&amp;\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\
\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}&amp;\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}}&amp;0\\
0&amp;(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\end{pmatrix}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}&amp;\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\
\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}&amp;\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}}&amp;0\\
0&amp;(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\end{pmatrix}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p">The diagonal factor in the block representation of <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}</annotation></semantics></math> contracts
<math id="A2.SS1.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> but leaves <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> unchanged. For an observable
<math id="A2.SS1.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, contraction therefore relies on the
<math id="A2.SS1.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>-component <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f</annotation></semantics></math> created by reflection. The next
subsection estimates this component and the subsequent action of
<math id="A2.SS1.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin with the reflection operator <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let
<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that
<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,y)=f(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,y)=f(y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Although <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> initially depends only on the auxiliary
coordinate <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, reflection gives <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{U}f)(x,y)=f(2x-y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{U}f)(x,y)=f(2x-y)</annotation></semantics></math>, which generally depends on both coordinates. Its macroscopic and microscopic
components are <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. The following
probabilistic representation identifies the squared norm of the microscopic
component created by reflection with an expected conditional variance, thereby
enabling quantitative estimate by the conditional Poincaré estimates used in
Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Concretely, under <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, write</p>
<table id="A2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}\coloneqq X+\sqrt{\eta}\,Z\,,\hskip 20.00003ptY_{-}\coloneqq X-\sqrt{\eta}\,Z\,,\hskip 20.00003ptZ\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)\,,\hskip 20.00003ptX\sim\mu\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}\coloneqq X+\sqrt{\eta}\,Z\,,\hskip 20.00003ptY_{-}\coloneqq X-\sqrt{\eta}\,Z\,,\hskip 20.00003ptZ\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)\,,\hskip 20.00003ptX\sim\mu\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The pair <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y_{+},Y_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y_{+},Y_{-})</annotation></semantics></math> is exchangeable. We henceforth identify
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> and write <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(y)</annotation></semantics></math> for a
macroscopic observable. Under this identification,</p>
<table id="A2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f)(y)=\mathbb{E}[f(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\mathbb{E}\Var(f(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f)(y)=\mathbb{E}[f(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\mathbb{E}\Var(f(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To quantify the microscopic component <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f</annotation></semantics></math> created when reflection
acts on <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})^{1/2}\hskip 10.00002pt\text{on }\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>on </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})^{1/2}\hskip 10.00002pt\text{on }\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">By (<a href="#A2.E5" title="Equation B.5 ‣ B.1 Operator framework and micro–macro decomposition ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>),
<math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence</p>
<table id="A2.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f\|\,,\hskip 10.00002ptf\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f\|\,,\hskip 10.00002ptf\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Thus a lower bound for <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> quantifies how much of a macroscopic
observable reflection transfers into the microscopic subspace.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Uniform macroscopic coercivity)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and set</span></p>
<table id="A2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\rm mac}\coloneqq\frac{1-\alpha\eta}{1+\alpha\eta}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\gamma_{\rm gap}\coloneqq\sqrt{1-\rho_{\rm mac}^{2}}=\frac{2\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}{1+\alpha\eta}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>mac</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>mac</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\rm mac}\coloneqq\frac{1-\alpha\eta}{1+\alpha\eta}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\gamma_{\rm gap}\coloneqq\sqrt{1-\rho_{\rm mac}^{2}}=\frac{2\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}{1+\alpha\eta}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Note that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\rm gap}\geq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\alpha\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\rm gap}\geq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\alpha\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the following hold.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(1) For every <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\in H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\in H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="4\eta\,\|\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}\leq\|f\|^{2}-\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝖴</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝖴</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝖴</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\eta\,\|\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}\leq\|f\|^{2}-\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(2) Consider the mean-zero macroscopic subspace <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\coloneqq\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\cap L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\coloneqq\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\cap L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\|\leq\rho_{\rm mac}\hskip 10.00002pt\text{and}\hskip 10.00002pt\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\succeq-\frac{1}{2}\,I\hskip 20.00003pt\text{on }\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>mac</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">on </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\|\leq\rho_{\rm mac}\hskip 10.00002pt\text{and}\hskip 10.00002pt\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\succeq-\frac{1}{2}\,I\hskip 20.00003pt\text{on }\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}=(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})^{1/2}\succeq\gamma_{\rm gap}I\hskip 20.00003pt\text{on }\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">on </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}=(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})^{1/2}\succeq\gamma_{\rm gap}I\hskip 20.00003pt\text{on }\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We prove <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> in
Appendix <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>. The identity
(<a href="#A2.E9" title="Equation B.9 ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.9</span></a>) expresses <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of the
conditional variance of <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(Y_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(Y_{-})</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. Differentiating the
corresponding conditional expectation shows that this variance controls how
quickly <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f</annotation></semantics></math> changes with <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. The Poincaré inequality for
<math id="A2.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> then bounds the norm of a centered <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of
<math id="A2.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|</annotation></semantics></math>, giving the stated estimate.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is boundedly invertible on <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math>,
(<a href="#A2.E11" title="Equation B.11 ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.11</span></a>) gives the polar decomposition</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\,:\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\longrightarrow\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\,:\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\longrightarrow\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> measures the size of the microscopic component created by
reflection, while the isometry <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> records its direction in
<math id="A2.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The next proposition says that the half-turn acts nearly as <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-I</annotation></semantics></math> on the
corresponding microscopic directions <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Global half-turn bound)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist universal constants <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c,C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c,C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that, if
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq c</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}v\bigr\|^{2}\leq C\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}v\|^{2}\,,\hskip 20.00003ptv\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}v\bigr\|^{2}\leq C\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}v\|^{2}\,,\hskip 20.00003ptv\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We prove <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> in
<a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sections</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> and <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Together, <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemmas</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>
provide the estimates used in the modified <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> argument below.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Modified <math id="A2.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> contraction and proof of the main theorem</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now prove <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 3.5 (𝜒^2 convergence). ‣ 3.3 Ideal Proximal BPS ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> using a discrete modified <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
argument. For <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math>, write</p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}f\,,\hskip 20.00003ptf_{\perp}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}^{\perp}f\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}f\,,\hskip 20.00003ptf_{\perp}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}^{\perp}f\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> are, respectively, the macroscopic
and microscopic parts of <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\rho\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\rho\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. The ordinary <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> energy does not by itself give
the required one-step contraction. Indeed, since <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}</annotation></semantics></math> is unitary and
<math id="A2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> is a contraction,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathsf{K}f\|^{2}-\|f\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathsf{K}f\|^{2}-\|f\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\rho)^{2}\,\|\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}f_{\perp}\|^{2}-\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\rho)^{2}\,\|\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}f_{\perp}\|^{2}-\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\rho\,(2-\rho)\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\leq-\rho\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\rho\,(2-\rho)\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\leq-\rho\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This estimate controls <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> but gives nothing when
<math id="A2.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=f_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=f_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Reflection moves part of <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> into the
microscopic subspace, but this transfer is not captured by the <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm,
which is a standard difficulty in hypocoercivity. The modified <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
method addresses this difficulty by adding a corrector to the Lyapunov
function. The corrector records the transfer from <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="A2.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>, allowing the contraction in
(<a href="#A2.E18" title="Equation B.18 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.18</span></a>) to also control <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This idea goes back to Dolbeault, Mouhot, and Schmeiser <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>; here we
follow the refinement of Fan, Li, and
Lu <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To construct the corrector, we first isolate the part of <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> that
couples to <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> under reflection. Define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{V}}\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{V}}\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">By (<a href="#A2.E16" title="Equation B.16 ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.16</span></a>),
<math id="A2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the component of
<math id="A2.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> orthogonal to <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{ran}(\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ran</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{ran}(\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}})</annotation></semantics></math> is annihilated by
<math id="A2.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an isometry,
<math id="A2.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> is the orthogonal
projection of <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> onto <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{ran}(\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ran</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{ran}(\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence
<math id="A2.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|\leq\|f_{\perp}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|\leq\|f_{\perp}\|</annotation></semantics></math>. We work with <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>, rather
than with this projection itself, because <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> both belong to <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math> and can therefore be
paired in the corrector.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">With this notation, let <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be a weight to be chosen below and
define the modified Lyapunov function</p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\coloneqq\|f\|^{2}+\omega\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\coloneqq\|f\|^{2}+\omega\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where the corrector is</p>
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})\coloneqq\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl(\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}-\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\bigr)-\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr\rangle\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})\coloneqq\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl(\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}-\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\bigr)-\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is applied only on <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A2.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\succeq\gamma_{\rm gap}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\succeq\gamma_{\rm gap}I</annotation></semantics></math>, so the corrector is well-defined.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To motivate this choice, recall from (<a href="#A2.E7" title="Equation B.7 ‣ B.1 Operator framework and micro–macro decomposition ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.7</span></a>) that
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}</annotation></semantics></math> acts in two stages: it first maps</p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{P}}+f_{\perp}\longmapsto f_{\mathsf{P}}+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}f_{\perp}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{P}}+f_{\perp}\longmapsto f_{\mathsf{P}}+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">and then applies <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the moment, set <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0</annotation></semantics></math> and replace
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The error
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> introduced by this replacement is controlled by
<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>. Denote the resulting idealized operator
by</p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}\coloneqq\mathsf{U}(\mathsf{P}-\mathsf{P}^{\perp})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}\coloneqq\mathsf{U}(\mathsf{P}-\mathsf{P}^{\perp})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Set <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\coloneqq\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\coloneqq\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the corresponding components by</p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}g\,,\hskip 20.00003ptg_{\mathsf{V}}\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}g\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}g\,,\hskip 20.00003ptg_{\mathsf{V}}\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}g\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p">In terms of these components, <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by the
operator-valued rotation matrix</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}g_{\mathsf{P}}\\
g_{\mathsf{V}}\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}&amp;-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\\
\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}&amp;\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}f_{\mathsf{P}}\\
f_{\mathsf{V}}\end{pmatrix}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}g_{\mathsf{P}}\\
g_{\mathsf{V}}\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}&amp;-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\\
\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}&amp;\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}f_{\mathsf{P}}\\
f_{\mathsf{V}}\end{pmatrix}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.5" class="ltx_p">Indeed, the first component follows immediately from the block representation
of <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}</annotation></semantics></math> and the polar decomposition
(<a href="#A2.E16" title="Equation B.16 ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.16</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathsf{P}\mathsf{U}(f_{\mathsf{P}}-f_{\perp})=\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}=\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}=\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯𝖴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathsf{P}\mathsf{U}(f_{\mathsf{P}}-f_{\perp})=\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}=\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}=\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.6" class="ltx_p">For the second component, substitute
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> into
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> from
(<a href="#A2.E5" title="Equation B.5 ‣ B.1 Operator framework and micro–macro decomposition ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>). Since <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> commutes with
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, this gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.7" class="ltx_p">The ranges of <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> lie in <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded. Applying <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> to the
displayed identity therefore gives
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{\mathsf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{\mathsf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\mathsf{U}(f_{\mathsf{P}}-f_{\perp})=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}(\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}f_{\perp})=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\mathsf{U}(f_{\mathsf{P}}-f_{\perp})=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}(\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}f_{\perp})=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.8" class="ltx_p">This proves the claimed matrix formula. Since
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I</annotation></semantics></math>, the block matrix acts as a rotation on
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\oplus\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\oplus\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under this rotation,
direct substitution into (<a href="#A2.E20" title="Equation B.20 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.20</span></a>) gives</p>
<table id="A2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{C}(g_{\mathsf{P}},g_{\mathsf{V}})-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{C}(g_{\mathsf{P}},g_{\mathsf{V}})-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt=\mathscr{C}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}\,,\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}})-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt=\mathscr{C}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}\,,\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}})-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt=-\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt=-\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.9" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\omega&lt;\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\omega&lt;\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, combining the leading terms from
(<a href="#A2.E18" title="Equation B.18 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.18</span></a>) and
(<a href="#A2.E21" title="Equation B.21 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.21</span></a>), and using
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|\leq\|f_{\perp}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|\leq\|f_{\perp}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, gives</p>
<table id="A2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\rho\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}+\omega\,\bigl(-\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\bigr)\leq-\omega\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}-(\rho-\omega)\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\rho\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}+\omega\,\bigl(-\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\bigr)\leq-\omega\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}-(\rho-\omega)\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.10" class="ltx_p">Thus the leading terms control both components. This calculation makes
explicit the role of the corrector in the modified <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> hypocoercivity
argument; see also Fan, Li, and Lu <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We now turn from the idealized calculation to the contraction proof. The
modified <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> argument has two steps: we first show that the Lyapunov
function is equivalent to the squared <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm and then establish its
one-step decay.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Equivalence with the squared <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\omega\leq\gamma_{\rm gap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\omega\leq\gamma_{\rm gap}</annotation></semantics></math>, then every
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\,\|f\|^{2}\leq\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\leq\frac{3}{2}\,\|f\|^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\,\|f\|^{2}\leq\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\leq\frac{3}{2}\,\|f\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">The operators <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> commute, so
<math id="A2.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is self-adjoint on
<math id="A2.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I+(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1})^{2}=I+\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-2}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I+(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1})^{2}=I+\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-2}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last identity uses <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I</annotation></semantics></math>.
By (<a href="#A2.E20" title="Equation B.20 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.20</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Bigl\langle\begin{pmatrix}f_{\mathsf{P}}\\
f_{\mathsf{V}}\end{pmatrix}\,,\begin{pmatrix}I&amp;-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\
-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&amp;-I\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}f_{\mathsf{P}}\\
f_{\mathsf{V}}\end{pmatrix}\Bigr\rangle\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Bigl\langle\begin{pmatrix}f_{\mathsf{P}}\\
f_{\mathsf{V}}\end{pmatrix}\,,\begin{pmatrix}I&amp;-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\
-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&amp;-I\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}f_{\mathsf{P}}\\
f_{\mathsf{V}}\end{pmatrix}\Bigr\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">The square of the block operator in this display is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}I&amp;-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\
-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&amp;-I\end{pmatrix}^{\!2}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-2}&amp;0\\
0&amp;\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-2}\end{pmatrix}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}I&amp;-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\
-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&amp;-I\end{pmatrix}^{\!2}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-2}&amp;0\\
0&amp;\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-2}\end{pmatrix}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since the block operator is self-adjoint and
<math id="A2.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\succeq\gamma_{\rm gap}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\succeq\gamma_{\rm gap}I</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Bigl\|\begin{pmatrix}I&amp;-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\
-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&amp;-I\end{pmatrix}\Bigr\|=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\|\leq\frac{1}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl\|\begin{pmatrix}I&amp;-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\
-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&amp;-I\end{pmatrix}\Bigr\|=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\|\leq\frac{1}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">Applying this operator norm bound to the preceding quadratic form gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})|\leq\frac{1}{2\gamma_{\rm gap}}\,\bigl(\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\bigr)\leq\frac{1}{2\gamma_{\rm gap}}\,\|f\|^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})|\leq\frac{1}{2\gamma_{\rm gap}}\,\bigl(\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\bigr)\leq\frac{1}{2\gamma_{\rm gap}}\,\|f\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">Here the second inequality uses <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\leq\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}=\|f\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\leq\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}=\|f\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, (<a href="#A2.E19" title="Equation B.19 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.19</span></a>),
(<a href="#A2.E23" title="Equation B.23 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.23</span></a>), and <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\leq\gamma_{\rm gap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\leq\gamma_{\rm gap}</annotation></semantics></math> imply</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl|\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)-\|f\|^{2}\bigr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl|\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)-\|f\|^{2}\bigr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\omega\,|\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})|\leq\frac{\omega}{2\gamma_{\rm gap}}\,\|f\|^{2}\leq\frac{1}{2}\,\|f\|^{2}\,.\qed" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\omega\,|\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})|\leq\frac{\omega}{2\gamma_{\rm gap}}\,\|f\|^{2}\leq\frac{1}{2}\,\|f\|^{2}\,.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(One-step decay of the Lyapunov function)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist universal constants <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\rm hyp},c_{0},c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\rm hyp},c_{0},c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that the
following holds. Set</span></p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\rho}\coloneqq\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})+\Bigl(\frac{\rho}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}\Bigr)^{2}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\omega\coloneqq\frac{c_{\rm hyp}\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\rho}\coloneqq\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})+\Bigl(\frac{\rho}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}\Bigr)^{2}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\omega\coloneqq\frac{c_{\rm hyp}\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, then every
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}f)\leq\Bigl(1-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}f)\leq\Bigl(1-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Take <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}\leq 1/16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}\leq 1/16</annotation></semantics></math>. Then
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\rm gap}\leq 2\sqrt{\alpha\eta}\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\rm gap}\leq 2\sqrt{\alpha\eta}\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, and consequently
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\rho}\geq\log 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\rho}\geq\log 2</annotation></semantics></math>.
We compare the actual update with the idealized operator analyzed above.
Let <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\coloneqq\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\coloneqq\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}g</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathsf{V}}\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathsf{V}}\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}g</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the definitions of <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{K}f-\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{K}f-\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathsf{U}\bigl[I+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathsf{U}\bigl[I+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathsf{U}\bigl[\rho f_{\perp}+(1-\rho)(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})f_{\perp}\bigr]\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathsf{U}\bigl[\rho f_{\perp}+(1-\rho)(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})f_{\perp}\bigr]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, the two components of
this difference are</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{P}(\mathsf{K}f-\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{P}(\mathsf{K}f-\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\bigl[I+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]f_{\perp}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\bigl[I+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]f_{\perp}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}(\mathsf{K}f-\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}(\mathsf{K}f-\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\bigl[I+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]f_{\perp}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\bigl[I+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]f_{\perp}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">The same vector therefore determines both components of the error. Denote
it by</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\rho}\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\bigl[I+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]f_{\perp}=\rho f_{\mathsf{V}}+(1-\rho)r\,,\hskip 20.00003ptr\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})f_{\perp}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\rho}\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\bigl[I+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]f_{\perp}=\rho f_{\mathsf{V}}+(1-\rho)r\,,\hskip 20.00003ptr\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})f_{\perp}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Both <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> belong to <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math>. In
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, the first
term comes from refreshment, while the second measures the departure of
the half turn from <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}}=g_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}=g_{\mathsf{V}}-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}}=g_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}=g_{\mathsf{V}}-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting (<a href="#A2.E27" title="Equation B.27 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.27</span></a>) into the definition
(<a href="#A2.E20" title="Equation B.20 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.20</span></a>) of the corrector <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and expanding
gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{C}\bigl((\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr)-\mathscr{C}(g_{\mathsf{P}},g_{\mathsf{V}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{C}\bigl((\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr)-\mathscr{C}(g_{\mathsf{P}},g_{\mathsf{V}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt=\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{V}},\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl(\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}-\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt=\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{V}},\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl(\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}-\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt\hskip 20.00003pt+{}\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle-\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho},g_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr\rangle+\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt\hskip 20.00003pt+{}\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle-\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho},g_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr\rangle+\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt=\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl(\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}+\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}\bigr)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt=\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl(\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}+\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}\bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">In the last equality, the two terms containing <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathsf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathsf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> cancel.
For the terms linear in <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the commutation of
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the identity
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I</annotation></semantics></math> give</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt=\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle=\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt=\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle=\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.7.1" class="ltx_text">The same identity reduces the quadratic terms to</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl(\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}+\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}\bigr)=\frac{1}{2}\,\|r_{\rho}\|^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl(\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}+\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}\bigr)=\frac{1}{2}\,\|r_{\rho}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.8.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, combined with (<a href="#A2.E21" title="Equation B.21 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.21</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{C}\bigl((\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr)-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{C}\bigl((\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr)-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt=\bigl[\mathscr{C}\bigl((\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr)-\mathscr{C}(g_{\mathsf{P}},g_{\mathsf{V}})\bigr]+\bigl[\mathscr{C}(g_{\mathsf{P}},g_{\mathsf{V}})-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt=\bigl[\mathscr{C}\bigl((\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr)-\mathscr{C}(g_{\mathsf{P}},g_{\mathsf{V}})\bigr]+\bigl[\mathscr{C}(g_{\mathsf{P}},g_{\mathsf{V}})-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt=-\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}+\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\frac{1}{2}\,\|r_{\rho}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt=-\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}+\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\frac{1}{2}\,\|r_{\rho}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.9.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, it remains to estimate <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}\coloneqq(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}\coloneqq(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.10.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\mathsf{L}^{*}f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖫</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\mathsf{L}^{*}f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>, applying
(<a href="#A2.E17" title="Equation B.17 ‣ Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.17</span></a>) to <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}v</annotation></semantics></math> and then taking
adjoints gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r\|^{2}=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})f_{\perp}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r\|^{2}=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})f_{\perp}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.11.1" class="ltx_text">Together with <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\succeq\gamma_{\rm gap}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\succeq\gamma_{\rm gap}I</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|\leq\|f_{\perp}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|\leq\|f_{\perp}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, this gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\rho^{2}\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}+2(1-\rho)^{2}\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r\|^{2}\leq C\Lambda_{\rho}\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\rho^{2}\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}+2(1-\rho)^{2}\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r\|^{2}\leq C\Lambda_{\rho}\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.12.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, since <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> are contractions, <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|r_{\rho}\|\leq\rho\,\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|+(1-\rho)\,\|r\|\leq 2\,\|f_{\perp}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|r_{\rho}\|\leq\rho\,\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|+(1-\rho)\,\|r\|\leq 2\,\|f_{\perp}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">The rotation formula for <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}\leq\|g_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|g_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}=\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}\leq\|g_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|g_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}=\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, Young’s inequality and
(<a href="#A2.E30" title="Equation B.30 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.30</span></a>) give</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl|\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle\bigr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl|\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle\bigr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{4}\,\|g_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{4}\,\|g_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{4}\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\frac{1}{4}\,\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}+C\Lambda_{\rho}\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{4}\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\frac{1}{4}\,\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}+C\Lambda_{\rho}\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Inserting these estimates into
(<a href="#A2.E28" title="Equation B.28 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.28</span></a>), and using
<math id="A2.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|\leq\|f_{\perp}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|\leq\|f_{\perp}\|</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\rho}\geq\log 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\rho}\geq\log 2</annotation></semantics></math>, gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E31X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{C}\bigl((\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr)-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})\leq-\frac{1}{2}\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+C\Lambda_{\rho}\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{C}\bigl((\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr)-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})\leq-\frac{1}{2}\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+C\Lambda_{\rho}\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(B.31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, (<a href="#A2.E18" title="Equation B.18 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.18</span></a>) and
(<a href="#A2.E31" title="Equation B.31 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.31</span></a>) give</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}f)-\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}f)-\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\rho\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}+\frac{c_{\rm hyp}\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\,\Bigl(-\frac{1}{2}\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+C\Lambda_{\rho}\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\rho\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}+\frac{c_{\rm hyp}\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\,\Bigl(-\frac{1}{2}\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+C\Lambda_{\rho}\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{c_{\rm hyp}\rho}{2\Lambda_{\rho}}\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}-(1-Cc_{\rm hyp})\,\rho\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{c_{\rm hyp}\rho}{2\Lambda_{\rho}}\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}-(1-Cc_{\rm hyp})\,\rho\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Choose <math id="A2.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\rm hyp}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\rm hyp}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently small so that
<math id="A2.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Cc_{\rm hyp}\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Cc_{\rm hyp}\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\rho}\geq\log 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\rho}\geq\log 2</annotation></semantics></math>, the last display is
then bounded above by</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\,\bigl(\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\bigr)=-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\,\|f\|^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\,\bigl(\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\bigr)=-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\,\|f\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to compare the last norm with the Lyapunov function. The
elementary inequality <math id="A2.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x/(a+x^{2})\leq 1/(2\sqrt{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x/(a+x^{2})\leq 1/(2\sqrt{a})</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A2.SS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\omega}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}=c_{\rm hyp}\,\frac{\rho/\gamma_{\rm gap}}{\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})+(\rho/\gamma_{\rm gap})^{2}}\leq\frac{c_{\rm hyp}}{2\sqrt{\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})}}\leq\frac{c_{\rm hyp}}{2\sqrt{\log 2}}\leq 1\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>ω</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\omega}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}=c_{\rm hyp}\,\frac{\rho/\gamma_{\rm gap}}{\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})+(\rho/\gamma_{\rm gap})^{2}}\leq\frac{c_{\rm hyp}}{2\sqrt{\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})}}\leq\frac{c_{\rm hyp}}{2\sqrt{\log 2}}\leq 1\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A2.SS3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\leq\gamma_{\rm gap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\leq\gamma_{\rm gap}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the upper bound in
<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3 (Equivalence with the squared 𝐿^2 norm). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f\|^{2}\geq\frac{2}{3}\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f\|^{2}\geq\frac{2}{3}\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p10.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p10.5.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}f)\leq\Bigl(1-\frac{2c\rho}{3\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}f)\leq\Bigl(1-\frac{2c\rho}{3\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p10.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p10.6.1" class="ltx_text">which is (<a href="#A2.E26" title="Equation B.26 ‣ Lemma B.4 (One-step decay of the Lyapunov function). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.26</span></a>) after renaming the universal
constant.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Combining
<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3 (Equivalence with the squared 𝐿^2 norm). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemmas</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4 (One-step decay of the Lyapunov function). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, we can now
prove the <math id="A2.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> contraction in <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 3.5 (𝜒^2 convergence). ‣ 3.3 Ideal Proximal BPS ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 3.5 (𝜒^2 convergence). ‣ 3.3 Ideal Proximal BPS ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first turn the one-step Lyapunov decay into a fixed <math id="A2.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> contraction
over a block of <math id="A2.SS3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> steps, and then apply this contraction to densities.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Take <math id="A2.SS3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> from <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4 (One-step decay of the Lyapunov function). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a> and choose a fixed
universal <math id="A2.SS3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\star}\in(0,1/2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\star}\in(0,1/2]</annotation></semantics></math>. The one-step estimate requires
<math id="A2.SS3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="A2.SS3.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\eta\leq\beta\eta\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\eta\leq\beta\eta\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\log(e/x)\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\log(e/x)\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS3.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;x\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;x\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the prescribed refreshment
probability satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\rho=\rho_{\star}\sqrt{\alpha\eta\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\leq\rho_{\star}\leq\frac{1}{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\rho=\rho_{\star}\sqrt{\alpha\eta\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\leq\rho_{\star}\leq\frac{1}{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">The decay rate in <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4 (One-step decay of the Lyapunov function). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a> is
<math id="A2.SS3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho/\Lambda_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho/\Lambda_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, so a fixed contraction is obtained by taking
<math id="A2.SS3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> proportional to <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\rho}/\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\rho}/\rho</annotation></semantics></math>. We first bound this ratio.
Recall that
<math id="A2.SS3.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\rm gap}\asymp\sqrt{\alpha\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo>≍</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\rm gap}\asymp\sqrt{\alpha\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\asymp\log(e/(\alpha\eta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≍</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\asymp\log(e/(\alpha\eta))</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Bigl(\frac{\rho}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}\Bigr)^{2}\leq C\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\rho\geq c\gamma_{\rm gap}\sqrt{\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl(\frac{\rho}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}\Bigr)^{2}\leq C\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\rho\geq c\gamma_{\rm gap}\sqrt{\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">It follows from the definition of <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\Lambda_{\rho}}{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mi>ρ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\Lambda_{\rho}}{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C\,\frac{\sqrt{\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})}}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}\leq\frac{C}{\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}\sqrt{\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C\,\frac{\sqrt{\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})}}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}\leq\frac{C}{\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}\sqrt{\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">Choose a sufficiently large universal constant <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and consider</span></p>
<table id="A2.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq C_{1}\,\frac{\Lambda_{\rho}}{\rho}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mi>ρ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq C_{1}\,\frac{\Lambda_{\rho}}{\rho}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p14.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p14.4.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math>, take <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> as in
(<a href="#A2.E25" title="Equation B.25 ‣ Lemma B.4 (One-step decay of the Lyapunov function). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.25</span></a>). Iterating
(<a href="#A2.E26" title="Equation B.26 ‣ Lemma B.4 (One-step decay of the Lyapunov function). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.26</span></a>) over this block gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}^{N}f)\leq\Bigl(1-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)^{N}\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}^{N}f)\leq\Bigl(1-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)^{N}\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p14.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p14.5.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the lower bound in (<a href="#A2.E22" title="Equation B.22 ‣ Lemma B.3 (Equivalence with the squared 𝐿^2 norm). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.22</span></a>) to
<math id="A2.SS3.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}^{N}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}^{N}f</annotation></semantics></math> and the upper bound to <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathsf{K}^{N}f\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathsf{K}^{N}f\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}^{N}f)\leq 2\,\Bigl(1-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)^{N}\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\leq 3\,\Bigl(1-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)^{N}\,\|f\|^{2}\leq 3e^{-cC_{1}}\,\|f\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}^{N}f)\leq 2\,\Bigl(1-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)^{N}\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\leq 3\,\Bigl(1-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)^{N}\,\|f\|^{2}\leq 3e^{-cC_{1}}\,\|f\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p14.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p14.6.1" class="ltx_text">The last step uses <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-x\leq e^{-x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-x\leq e^{-x}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p14.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq C_{1}\Lambda_{\rho}/\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq C_{1}\Lambda_{\rho}/\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.
Taking <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently large makes <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3e^{-cC_{1}}\leq e^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3e^{-cC_{1}}\leq e^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathsf{K}^{N}f\|^{2}\leq e^{-1}\,\|f\|^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{K}^{N}f\|^{2}\leq e^{-1}\,\|f\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p14.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p14.7.1" class="ltx_text">Iterating by blocks, the <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> contraction
(<a href="#A2.E33" title="Equation B.33 ‣ Proof of . ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.33</span></a>) is equivalently, by (<a href="#A4.E5" title="Equation D.5 ‣ D.1 Hilbert space and Markov operator conventions ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a>) and the
adjoint remark following it, the <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-estimate</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\chi^{2}\bigl(\nu_{0}\mathcal{K}^{JN}\|\pi_{\eta}\bigr)\leq e^{-J}\chi^{2}(\nu_{0}\|\pi_{\eta})\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}\bigl(\nu_{0}\mathcal{K}^{JN}\|\pi_{\eta}\bigr)\leq e^{-J}\chi^{2}(\nu_{0}\|\pi_{\eta})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p14.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p14.8.1" class="ltx_text">which proves (<a href="#S3.E14" title="Equation 3.14 ‣ Theorem 3.5 (𝜒^2 convergence). ‣ 3.3 Ideal Proximal BPS ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.14</span></a>). The <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>-marginal of
<math id="A2.SS3.p14.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, and total variation cannot increase under
projection. Moreover, Cauchy–Schwarz gives
<math id="A2.SS3.p14.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{TV}(P,Q)\leq\tfrac{1}{2}\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P\|Q)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>χ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{TV}(P,Q)\leq\tfrac{1}{2}\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P\|Q)}</annotation></semantics></math>, which gives (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 3.15 ‣ Theorem 3.5 (𝜒^2 convergence). ‣ 3.3 Ideal Proximal BPS ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.15</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix establishes the two model-specific estimates used by the
modified <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> method argument of Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>: the
macroscopic coercivity lemma
(<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>) and the global half-turn bound
(<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Proof of
<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first prove
(<a href="#A2.E13" title="Equation B.13 ‣ Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.13</span></a>). It suffices to consider
<math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in C_{\rm c}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in C_{\rm c}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, the general case following by density and
closedness of the gradient.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that the conditional
density <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}=y</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{y}(u)\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V((y+u)/2)-\frac{\|y-u\|^{2}}{8\eta}\Bigr\}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{y}(u)\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V((y+u)/2)-\frac{\|y-u\|^{2}}{8\eta}\Bigr\}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">and define</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s_{y}(u)\coloneqq-\frac{1}{2}\,\nabla V((y+u)/2)-\frac{y-u}{4\eta}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≔</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.317em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{y}(u)\coloneqq-\frac{1}{2}\,\nabla V((y+u)/2)-\frac{y-u}{4\eta}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Differentiating the normalized conditional density gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f(y)=\mathrm{Cov}\bigl(f(Y_{-}),s_{y}(Y_{-})\bigm|Y_{+}=y\bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f(y)=\mathrm{Cov}\bigl(f(Y_{-}),s_{y}(Y_{-})\bigm|Y_{+}=y\bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The negative log-density of <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> has Hessian</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{4}\,\bigl\{\nabla^{2}V((y+u)/2)+\eta^{-1}I\bigr\}\succeq\frac{\alpha+\eta^{-1}}{4}\,I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{4}\,\bigl\{\nabla^{2}V((y+u)/2)+\eta^{-1}I\bigr\}\succeq\frac{\alpha+\eta^{-1}}{4}\,I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, the conditional Poincaré inequality implies, for every unit
vector <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Var\bigl(a^{\top}s_{y}(Y_{-})\bigm|Y_{+}=y\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Var\bigl(a^{\top}s_{y}(Y_{-})\bigm|Y_{+}=y\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{4}{\alpha+\eta^{-1}}\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\nabla_{u}(a^{\top}s_{y})(Y_{-})\|^{2}\,\bigm|\,Y_{+}=y\bigr]\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.317em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{4}{\alpha+\eta^{-1}}\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\nabla_{u}(a^{\top}s_{y})(Y_{-})\|^{2}\,\bigm|\,Y_{+}=y\bigr]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">The assumptions
<math id="A3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq\beta I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq\beta I</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> give</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{u}s_{y}(u)\|_{\rm op}\leq\frac{\eta^{-1}-\alpha}{4}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{u}s_{y}(u)\|_{\rm op}\leq\frac{\eta^{-1}-\alpha}{4}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Var\bigl(a^{\top}s_{y}(Y_{-})\bigm|Y_{+}=y\bigr)\leq\frac{(\eta^{-1}-\alpha)^{2}}{4\,(\alpha+\eta^{-1})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Var\bigl(a^{\top}s_{y}(Y_{-})\bigm|Y_{+}=y\bigr)\leq\frac{(\eta^{-1}-\alpha)^{2}}{4\,(\alpha+\eta^{-1})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Applying conditional Cauchy–Schwarz in
(<a href="#A3.E1" title="Equation C.1 ‣ Proof of . ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>) and taking the supremum over
<math id="A3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|a\|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|a\|=1</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f(y)\|^{2}\leq\frac{(\eta^{-1}-\alpha)^{2}}{4\,(\alpha+\eta^{-1})}\Var(f(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi mathsize="0.900em">Var</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f(y)\|^{2}\leq\frac{(\eta^{-1}-\alpha)^{2}}{4\,(\alpha+\eta^{-1})}\Var(f(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">Integrating in <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and using (<a href="#A2.E9" title="Equation B.9 ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.9</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\eta\,\|\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}\leq\frac{(1-\alpha\eta)^{2}}{4\,(1+\alpha\eta)}\,\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝖴</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝖴</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta\,\|\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}\leq\frac{(1-\alpha\eta)^{2}}{4\,(1+\alpha\eta)}\,\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">Finally,
<math id="A3.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\|f\|^{2}-\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\|f\|^{2}-\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which proves (<a href="#A2.E13" title="Equation B.13 ‣ Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.13</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We next bound the spectrum of <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> preserves constants, <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f</annotation></semantics></math> is centered.
The Poincaré inequality for the marginal law <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\Var_{\pi_{\eta}^{Y}}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f)\leq\Bigl(\frac{1}{\alpha}+\eta\Bigr)\,\|\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">Var</mi><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\Var_{\pi_{\eta}^{Y}}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f)\leq\Bigl(\frac{1}{\alpha}+\eta\Bigr)\,\|\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Combining (<a href="#A3.E3" title="Equation C.3 ‣ Proof of . ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>) with
(<a href="#A3.E2" title="Equation C.2 ‣ Proof of . ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>) and rearranging gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|\leq\frac{1-\alpha\eta}{1+\alpha\eta}\,\|f\|=\rho_{\rm mac}\,\|f\|\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>mac</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|\leq\frac{1-\alpha\eta}{1+\alpha\eta}\,\|f\|=\rho_{\rm mac}\,\|f\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is self-adjoint, this proves</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\rho_{\rm mac}I\preceq\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\preceq\rho_{\rm mac}I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>mac</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>mac</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\rho_{\rm mac}I\preceq\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\preceq\rho_{\rm mac}I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">It remains only to obtain the uniform lower bound
<math id="A3.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\succeq-\frac{1}{2}\,I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\succeq-\frac{1}{2}\,I</annotation></semantics></math>.
For every <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math>, exchangeability and
(<a href="#A2.E8" title="Equation B.8 ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a>) give</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl\langle g,(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})g\bigr\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl\langle g,(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})g\bigr\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\bigl(g(Y_{+})-g(Y_{-})\bigr)^{2}\bigr]=\frac{1}{2}\,\mathbb{E}_{X}\mathbb{E}_{Z}\bigl[\bigl(g(X+\sqrt{\eta}Z)-g(X-\sqrt{\eta}Z)\bigr)^{2}\bigr]\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\bigl(g(Y_{+})-g(Y_{-})\bigr)^{2}\bigr]=\frac{1}{2}\,\mathbb{E}_{X}\mathbb{E}_{Z}\bigl[\bigl(g(X+\sqrt{\eta}Z)-g(X-\sqrt{\eta}Z)\bigr)^{2}\bigr]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">For fixed <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=x</annotation></semantics></math>, the Gaussian Poincaré inequality implies</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{Z}\bigl[\bigl(g(x+\sqrt{\eta}Z)-g(x-\sqrt{\eta}Z)\bigr)^{2}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{Z}\bigl[\bigl(g(x+\sqrt{\eta}Z)-g(x-\sqrt{\eta}Z)\bigr)^{2}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\eta\,\mathbb{E}_{Z}\bigl\|\nabla g(x+\sqrt{\eta}Z)+\nabla g(x-\sqrt{\eta}Z)\bigr\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\eta\,\mathbb{E}_{Z}\bigl\|\nabla g(x+\sqrt{\eta}Z)+\nabla g(x-\sqrt{\eta}Z)\bigr\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">Averaging in <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and using that <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> have the same
marginal gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl\langle g,(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})g\bigr\rangle\leq 2\eta\,\|\nabla g\|^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\langle g,(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})g\bigr\rangle\leq 2\eta\,\|\nabla g\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying (<a href="#A3.E6" title="Equation C.6 ‣ Proof of . ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a>) with <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f</annotation></semantics></math> and using
(<a href="#A2.E13" title="Equation B.13 ‣ Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.13</span></a>), we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl\langle f,\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})f\bigr\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl\langle f,\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})f\bigr\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f,(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\bigr\rangle\leq 2\eta\,\|\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}\leq\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl\langle f,(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})f\bigr\rangle\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>f</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f,(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\bigr\rangle\leq 2\eta\,\|\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}\leq\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl\langle f,(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})f\bigr\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, as an operator inequality, <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})\preceq I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})\preceq I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
or equivalently</span></p>
<table id="A3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})^{2}(I+2\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})\succeq 0\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})^{2}(I+2\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})\succeq 0\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a self-adjoint contraction, its spectrum lies in
<math id="A3.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The scalar inequality corresponding to
(<a href="#A3.E7" title="Equation C.7 ‣ Proof of . ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.7</span></a>) is</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\lambda)^{2}(1+2\lambda)\geq 0\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\lambda\in\operatorname{Spec}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\lambda)^{2}(1+2\lambda)\geq 0\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\lambda\in\operatorname{Spec}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">and therefore <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{Spec}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})\subseteq[-1/2,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Spec}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})\subseteq[-1/2,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence
<math id="A3.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{1}{2}I\,\preceq\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.428em">⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{1}{2}I\,\preceq\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Together with (<a href="#A3.E4" title="Equation C.4 ‣ Proof of . ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>), this proves
(<a href="#A2.E14" title="Equation B.14 ‣ Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.14</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}\succeq(1-\rho_{\rm mac}^{2})\,I=\frac{4\alpha\eta}{(1+\alpha\eta)^{2}}\,I\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>mac</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}\succeq(1-\rho_{\rm mac}^{2})\,I=\frac{4\alpha\eta}{(1+\alpha\eta)^{2}}\,I\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">and therefore</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\succeq\frac{2\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}{1+\alpha\eta}\,I=\gamma_{\rm gap}I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\succeq\frac{2\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}{1+\alpha\eta}\,I=\gamma_{\rm gap}I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">This proves (<a href="#A2.E15" title="Equation B.15 ‣ Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.15</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The half-turn analysis below uses the following alternative form of
(<a href="#A3.E1" title="Equation C.1 ‣ Proof of . ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Derivative formula for <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>-almost every <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f(y)=\mathbb{E}[\nabla f(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]-\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),\nabla V(X)\mid Y_{+}=y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f(y)=\mathbb{E}[\nabla f(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]-\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),\nabla V(X)\mid Y_{+}=y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">First let <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in C_{\rm c}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in C_{\rm c}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>. The representation
(<a href="#A3.E1" title="Equation C.1 ‣ Proof of . ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f(y)=\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),s_{y}(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f(y)=\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),s_{y}(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using the definition of <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, we write</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s_{y}(u)=\Bigl\{\frac{1}{2}\nabla V((y+u)/2)-\frac{y-u}{4\eta}\Bigr\}-\nabla V((y+u)/2)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{y}(u)=\Bigl\{\frac{1}{2}\nabla V((y+u)/2)-\frac{y-u}{4\eta}\Bigr\}-\nabla V((y+u)/2)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">To rewrite (<a href="#A3.E1" title="Equation C.1 ‣ Proof of . ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>) in the claimed form, we
only need to identify the covariance generated by the vector in braces.
Integration by parts in <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> against the conditional density <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\nabla f(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]=\mathbb{E}\Bigl[f(Y_{-})\,\Bigl\{\frac{1}{2}\nabla V(X)-\frac{y-Y_{-}}{4\eta}\Bigr\}\ \Bigm|\ Y_{+}=y\Bigr]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.500em">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\nabla f(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]=\mathbb{E}\Bigl[f(Y_{-})\,\Bigl\{\frac{1}{2}\nabla V(X)-\frac{y-Y_{-}}{4\eta}\Bigr\}\ \Bigm|\ Y_{+}=y\Bigr]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Applying (<a href="#A3.E9" title="Equation C.9 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a>) to <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>, justified by compactly
supported cutoffs converging to <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\frac{1}{2}\nabla V(X)-\frac{y-Y_{-}}{4\eta}\,\Bigm|\,Y_{+}=y\Bigr]=0\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo fence="false" lspace="0.150em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.317em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\frac{1}{2}\nabla V(X)-\frac{y-Y_{-}}{4\eta}\,\Bigm|\,Y_{+}=y\Bigr]=0\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">Combining this with (<a href="#A3.E9" title="Equation C.9 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a>), we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f(y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{Cov}\Bigl(f(Y_{-}),\frac{1}{2}\nabla V(X)-\frac{y-Y_{-}}{4\eta}\,\Bigm|\,Y_{+}=y\Bigr)-\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),\nabla V(X)\mid Y_{+}=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" lspace="0.150em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.317em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{Cov}\Bigl(f(Y_{-}),\frac{1}{2}\nabla V(X)-\frac{y-Y_{-}}{4\eta}\,\Bigm|\,Y_{+}=y\Bigr)-\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),\nabla V(X)\mid Y_{+}=y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Bigl[f(Y_{-})\,\Bigl\{\frac{1}{2}\nabla V(X)-\frac{y-Y_{-}}{4\eta}\Bigr\}\,\Bigm|\,Y_{+}=y\Bigr]-\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),\nabla V(X)\mid Y_{+}=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.317em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Bigl[f(Y_{-})\,\Bigl\{\frac{1}{2}\nabla V(X)-\frac{y-Y_{-}}{4\eta}\Bigr\}\,\Bigm|\,Y_{+}=y\Bigr]-\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),\nabla V(X)\mid Y_{+}=y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\nabla f(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]-\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),\nabla V(X)\mid Y_{+}=y)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\nabla f(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]-\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),\nabla V(X)\mid Y_{+}=y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">This is (<a href="#A3.E8" title="Equation C.8 ‣ Lemma C.1 (Derivative formula for 𝖴_𝖯𝖯). ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a>) for smooth <math id="A3.SS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">The extension to <math id="A3.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> is a standard approximation
argument once we check that the covariance term is continuous in
<math id="A3.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. By (<a href="#S2.E11" title="Equation 2.11 ‣ Item (i) ‣ Proposition 2.1 (Geometry of the joint law). ‣ 2.2 Proximal augmentation and the restricted Gaussian oracle ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.11</span></a>), the conditional
law of <math id="A3.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A3.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}=y</annotation></semantics></math> has Poincaré constant at most
<math id="A3.SS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta/(1+\alpha\eta)\leq\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta/(1+\alpha\eta)\leq\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, for every unit vector
<math id="A3.SS1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Var(a^{\top}\nabla V(X)\mid Y_{+}=y)\leq\eta\,\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla^{2}V(X)\,a\|^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]\leq\beta^{2}\eta\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Var</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Var(a^{\top}\nabla V(X)\mid Y_{+}=y)\leq\eta\,\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla^{2}V(X)\,a\|^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]\leq\beta^{2}\eta\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Conditional Cauchy–Schwarz and
(<a href="#A2.E9" title="Equation B.9 ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.9</span></a>) therefore imply</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl\|\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),\nabla V(X)\mid Y_{+})\bigr\|_{L^{2}}\leq\beta\sqrt{\eta}\,\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\|\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),\nabla V(X)\mid Y_{+})\bigr\|_{L^{2}}\leq\beta\sqrt{\eta}\,\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">and the same bound applies to differences. Conditional expectation is
an <math id="A3.SS1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> contraction, and (<a href="#A2.E13" title="Equation B.13 ‣ Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.13</span></a>) controls the
left side. Thus every term in (<a href="#A3.E8" title="Equation C.8 ‣ Lemma C.1 (Derivative formula for 𝖴_𝖯𝖯). ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a>) is
continuous under <math id="A3.SS1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> approximation. Density of
<math id="A3.SS1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\rm c}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\rm c}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A3.SS1.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>The half-turn operator on affine functions</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This subsection establishes a conditional half-turn estimate for affine
observables. After rescaling <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X-y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X-y</annotation></semantics></math> by the Gaussian scale
<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we show that the half-turn nearly maps every affine
function with mean zero to its negative. The proof combines a Duhamel
representation of the half-turn with covariance identities for the
rescaled conditional law.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>, this estimate will be applied to
the conditional affine part of <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w</annotation></semantics></math> in the proof of
<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We first fix <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and work under the conditional law of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>
given <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=y</annotation></semantics></math>. The bounds below are uniform in <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and will later be
integrated over <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. To put the Gaussian confinement and harmonic
dynamics on unit scale, set</p>
<table id="A3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\coloneqq\frac{X-y}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,,\hskip 20.00003ptq_{y}\coloneqq\Law(W\mid Y=y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\coloneqq\frac{X-y}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,,\hskip 20.00003ptq_{y}\coloneqq\Law(W\mid Y=y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The density of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and the scaled potential gradient are</p>
<table id="A3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{y}(\mathrm{d}w)\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V(y+\sqrt{\eta}w)-\frac{1}{2}\|w\|^{2}\Bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}w\,,\hskip 20.00003ptg_{y}(w)\coloneqq\sqrt{\eta}\,\nabla V(y+\sqrt{\eta}w)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.317em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}(\mathrm{d}w)\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V(y+\sqrt{\eta}w)-\frac{1}{2}\|w\|^{2}\Bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}w\,,\hskip 20.00003ptg_{y}(w)\coloneqq\sqrt{\eta}\,\nabla V(y+\sqrt{\eta}w)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, the negative log-density of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> has Hessian
<math id="A3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I+\nabla g_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I+\nabla g_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
<table id="A3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\log q_{y}(w)=-(w+g_{y}(w))\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\alpha\eta I\preceq\nabla g_{y}(w)\preceq\beta\eta I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\log q_{y}(w)=-(w+g_{y}(w))\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\alpha\eta I\preceq\nabla g_{y}(w)\preceq\beta\eta I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">In particular, <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly log-concave. We use the same
symbol <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> for the conditional half-turn operator in the
normalized coordinate <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=(x-y)/\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=(x-y)/\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{H}_{y}f)(w)\coloneqq\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f\Bigl(\frac{x^{\prime}-y}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)\,\mathcal{H}_{y}(y+\sqrt{\eta}w,\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{H}_{y}f)(w)\coloneqq\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f\Bigl(\frac{x^{\prime}-y}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)\,\mathcal{H}_{y}(y+\sqrt{\eta}w,\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p">By <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 3.2 (Reversibility of the conditional half-turn kernel). ‣ 3.2 The ideal conditional half-turn process ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is a self-adjoint Markov
contraction on <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(q_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(q_{y})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Put</p>
<table id="A3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{w}_{y}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}W\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\Sigma_{y}\coloneqq\mathrm{Cov}_{q_{y}}(W)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{w}_{y}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}W\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\Sigma_{y}\coloneqq\mathrm{Cov}_{q_{y}}(W)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is the conditional covariance in the normalized
coordinate; equivalently, we have the identity
<math id="A3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)=\eta\Sigma_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)=\eta\Sigma_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Accordingly,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I-\Sigma_{y}=\eta\nabla^{2}U_{\eta}(y)\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I-\Sigma_{y}=\eta\nabla^{2}U_{\eta}(y)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">by (<a href="#A4.E10" title="Equation D.10 ‣ Hessian of the augmented marginal. ‣ D.2 Strong log-concavity and covariance bounds ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.10</span></a>). Thus <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I-\Sigma_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I-\Sigma_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is both the covariance
defect relative to a standard Gaussian and the normalized curvature of
the <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>-marginal. For <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, write
<math id="A3.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{a,y}:w\mapsto a^{\top}(w-\bar{w}_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{a,y}:w\mapsto a^{\top}(w-\bar{w}_{y})</annotation></semantics></math>; this affine function has mean zero
under <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The main result of this subsection is the following estimate.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Weighted half-turn estimate for affine functions)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Uniformly in <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, every
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{a,y}:w\mapsto a^{\top}(w-\bar{w}_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{a,y}:w\mapsto a^{\top}(w-\bar{w}_{y})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{y})\ell_{a,y}\|_{L^{2}(q_{y})}^{2}\leq C\beta\eta\,a^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{y})\ell_{a,y}\|_{L^{2}(q_{y})}^{2}\leq C\beta\eta\,a^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">More generally, suppose that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\mapsto a_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\mapsto a_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is measurable and
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and define</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(x,y)\coloneqq a_{y}^{\top}\Bigl(\frac{x-y}{\sqrt{\eta}}-\bar{w}_{y}\Bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(x,y)\coloneqq a_{y}^{\top}\Bigl(\frac{x-y}{\sqrt{\eta}}-\bar{w}_{y}\Bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\ell\|^{2}\leq C\beta\eta\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\ell\|^{2}\leq C\beta\eta\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We prove the proposition after two preparatory results. The first gives a
Duhamel representation of the deviation from exact sign reversal; the
second bounds the resulting term in terms of <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I-\Sigma_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I-\Sigma_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">To analyze <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{y}\ell_{a,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{y}\ell_{a,y}</annotation></semantics></math>, first fix a reference point
<math id="A3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{w}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{w}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> in the rescaled coordinate. The resulting
phase-space process is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}\dot{w}=p\,,\qquad\dot{p}=-\{w+g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}\,,\\
\text{event rate }[p^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}]_{+}\,,\\
p\longmapsto R_{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})}p\quad\text{at a bounce}\,.\end{gathered}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.300em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">˙</mo></mover><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.300em">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mtext>event rate </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.000em;" width="2.000em"></mspace><mtext>at a bounce</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0.300em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{gathered}\dot{w}=p\,,\qquad\dot{p}=-\{w+g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}\,,\\
\text{event rate }[p^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}]_{+}\,,\\
p\longmapsto R_{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})}p\quad\text{at a bounce}\,.\end{gathered}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p">The construction and path reversal arguments of
Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> apply verbatim, with phase space
law <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote the resulting strongly continuous
contraction semigroup by
<math id="A3.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>. On smooth compactly
supported observables, its generator is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}f(w,p)&amp;\coloneqq p^{\top}\nabla_{w}f(w,p)-\{w+g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}^{\top}\nabla_{p}f(w,p)\\
&amp;\qquad{}+[p^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}]_{+}\bigl\{f(w,R_{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})}p)-f(w,p)\bigr\}\,.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.022em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}f(w,p)&amp;\coloneqq p^{\top}\nabla_{w}f(w,p)-\{w+g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}^{\top}\nabla_{p}f(w,p)\\
&amp;\qquad{}+[p^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}]_{+}\bigl\{f(w,R_{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})}p)-f(w,p)\bigr\}\,.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p">The operator <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is
recovered by drawing <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}\sim q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}\sim q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, running the corresponding
process for time <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, and averaging over <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}</annotation></semantics></math> and the
initial Gaussian momentum.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{y}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{y}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}=\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}=\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{w}_{y}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{w}_{y}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and the bounce
rate vanishes. The dynamics reduce to harmonic motion,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}=w_{0}\cos t+p_{0}\sin t\,,\hskip 20.00003ptp_{t}=-w_{0}\sin t+p_{0}\cos t\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}=w_{0}\cos t+p_{0}\sin t\,,\hskip 20.00003ptp_{t}=-w_{0}\sin t+p_{0}\cos t\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p">so <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{a,y}(w_{\pi})=-\ell_{a,y}(w_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{a,y}(w_{\pi})=-\ell_{a,y}(w_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. For general <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, the
discrepancy between the harmonic center <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})</annotation></semantics></math> and the
conditional mean <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{w}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{w}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, together with the residual gradient
bounces, produces an inhomogeneous term. The next lemma identifies this
term.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.3</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Affine Duhamel formula)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{w}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{w}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, set</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{a,\widetilde{w}}(w,p)\coloneqq-a^{\top}\{\bar{w}_{y}+g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}-2\,[p^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}]_{+}^{2}\,\frac{a^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}}{\|g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\|^{2}}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{a,\widetilde{w}}(w,p)\coloneqq-a^{\top}\{\bar{w}_{y}+g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}-2\,[p^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}]_{+}^{2}\,\frac{a^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}}{\|g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\|^{2}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the quotient is defined as zero when
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{y}(w)=g_{y}(\widetilde{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{y}(w)=g_{y}(\widetilde{w})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\in L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\in L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))</annotation></semantics></math>, and for every
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}\ell_{a,y}=\ell_{a,y}\cos t+a^{\top}p\sin t+\int_{0}^{t}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\sin(t-s)\,\mathrm{d}s" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}\ell_{a,y}=\ell_{a,y}\cos t+a^{\top}p\sin t+\int_{0}^{t}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\sin(t-s)\,\mathrm{d}s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">in <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I+\mathsf{T}_{\pi}^{y,\widetilde{w}})\ell_{a,y}=\int_{0}^{\pi}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\sin s\,\mathrm{d}s\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I+\mathsf{T}_{\pi}^{y,\widetilde{w}})\ell_{a,y}=\int_{0}^{\pi}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\sin s\,\mathrm{d}s\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">The generator maps the position observable <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{a,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{a,y}</annotation></semantics></math> to the
momentum observable <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\top}p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\top}p</annotation></semantics></math>, and maps <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\top}p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\top}p</annotation></semantics></math> back to
<math id="A3.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\widetilde{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\widetilde{w}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, this pair evolves as a harmonic
system with the additional term <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{a,\widetilde{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{a,\widetilde{w}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and variation of
constants gives the claimed formula. We first establish the required
<math id="A3.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> bounds and justify these generator identities for the unbounded
observables.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{a,\widetilde{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{a,\widetilde{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> is square integrable. Its first term is
constant in <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(w,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(w,p)</annotation></semantics></math>, while the absolute value of its second term is at
most</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\,[p^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}]_{+}^{2}\,\frac{|a^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}|}{\|g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\|^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\,[p^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}]_{+}^{2}\,\frac{|a^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}|}{\|g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\,\|a\|\,\|p\|^{2}\,\|g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\,\|a\|\,\|p\|^{2}\,\|g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\beta\eta\,\|a\|\,\|p\|^{2}\,\|w-\widetilde{w}\|\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\beta\eta\,\|a\|\,\|p\|^{2}\,\|w-\widetilde{w}\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly log-concave and the momentum is Gaussian,
this bound shows that <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{a,\widetilde{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{a,\widetilde{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to
<math id="A3.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))</annotation></semantics></math>. The same moment bounds give
<math id="A3.SS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{a,y},a^{\top}p\in L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{a,y},a^{\top}p\in L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using
<math id="A3.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a^{\top}(R_{h}p-p)=-2(p^{\top}h)(a^{\top}h)/\|h\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\top}(R_{h}p-p)=-2(p^{\top}h)(a^{\top}h)/\|h\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[u]_{+}u=[u]_{+}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[u]_{+}u=[u]_{+}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the generator formula gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}\ell_{a,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}\ell_{a,y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=a^{\top}p\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}(a^{\top}p)=-\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=a^{\top}p\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}(a^{\top}p)=-\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">To justify these identities for the unbounded observables, set <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\widetilde{w}}(w,p)\coloneqq\frac{1}{2}\,\{\|w+g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\|^{2}+\|p\|^{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\widetilde{w}}(w,p)\coloneqq\frac{1}{2}\,\{\|w+g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\|^{2}+\|p\|^{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which is preserved by both the flow and the bounces. Let <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be
a smooth cutoff equal to one on <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,R]</annotation></semantics></math> and zero on
<math id="A3.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[2R,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[2R,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. Conservation of <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\widetilde{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\widetilde{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> gives, for
<math id="A3.SS2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in\{\ell_{a,y},a^{\top}p\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in\{\ell_{a,y},a^{\top}p\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A3.SS2.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}\{\chi_{R}(H_{\widetilde{w}})F\}=\chi_{R}(H_{\widetilde{w}})\,\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}\{\chi_{R}(H_{\widetilde{w}})F\}=\chi_{R}(H_{\widetilde{w}})\,\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}F</annotation></semantics></math>.
Applying Dynkin’s formula and then letting <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
using the preceding integrability bounds and semigroup contractivity,
yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}\ell_{a,y}-\ell_{a,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}\ell_{a,y}-\ell_{a,y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}(a^{\top}p)\,\mathrm{d}s\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}(a^{\top}p)\,\mathrm{d}s\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}(a^{\top}p)-a^{\top}p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}(a^{\top}p)-a^{\top}p</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}(-\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\widetilde{w}})\,\mathrm{d}s\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}(-\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\widetilde{w}})\,\mathrm{d}s\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">Applying variation of constants to this integral system gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}\ell_{a,y}=\ell_{a,y}\cos t+a^{\top}p\sin t+\int_{0}^{t}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\sin(t-s)\,\mathrm{d}s\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}\ell_{a,y}=\ell_{a,y}\cos t+a^{\top}p\sin t+\int_{0}^{t}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\sin(t-s)\,\mathrm{d}s\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">This is the first identity in the lemma. At <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, the homogeneous
part is <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\ell_{a,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\ell_{a,y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sin(\pi-s)=\sin s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sin(\pi-s)=\sin s</annotation></semantics></math>, which gives
(<a href="#A3.E12" title="Equation C.12 ‣ Lemma C.3 (Affine Duhamel formula). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.12</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition C.2 (Weighted half-turn estimate for affine functions). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> will also use the
following identities and bounds.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.4</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Conditional gradient covariance bound)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and assume <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Then
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}g_{y}(W)=-\bar{w}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}g_{y}(W)=-\bar{w}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="A3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}_{q_{y}}(W,g_{y}(W))=I-\Sigma_{y}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathrm{Cov}_{q_{y}}(g_{y}(W))\preceq\frac{\beta\eta}{1-\beta\eta}\,(I-\Sigma_{y})\preceq 2\beta\eta\,(I-\Sigma_{y})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}_{q_{y}}(W,g_{y}(W))=I-\Sigma_{y}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathrm{Cov}_{q_{y}}(g_{y}(W))\preceq\frac{\beta\eta}{1-\beta\eta}\,(I-\Sigma_{y})\preceq 2\beta\eta\,(I-\Sigma_{y})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under <math id="A3.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}=y</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=y+\sqrt{\eta}W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=y+\sqrt{\eta}W</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{-}=y+2\sqrt{\eta}W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{-}=y+2\sqrt{\eta}W</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying (<a href="#A3.E9" title="Equation C.9 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a>) to
<math id="A3.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:u\mapsto F((u-y)/(2\sqrt{\eta}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:u\mapsto F((u-y)/(2\sqrt{\eta}))</annotation></semantics></math> therefore gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}\nabla F(W)=\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}[F(W)\,\{W+g_{y}(W)\}]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}\nabla F(W)=\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}[F(W)\,\{W+g_{y}(W)\}]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking <math id="A3.SS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math> and then the coordinate functions of <math id="A3.SS2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{y}(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{y}(W)</annotation></semantics></math>, with the same cutoff approximation as in
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1 (Derivative formula for 𝖴_𝖯𝖯). ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}g_{y}(W)=-\bar{w}_{y}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathrm{Cov}(W,g_{y}(W))=I-\Sigma_{y}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathbb{E}\nabla g_{y}(W)=I-\Sigma_{y}+\mathrm{Cov}(g_{y}(W))\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}g_{y}(W)=-\bar{w}_{y}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathrm{Cov}(W,g_{y}(W))=I-\Sigma_{y}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathbb{E}\nabla g_{y}(W)=I-\Sigma_{y}+\mathrm{Cov}(g_{y}(W))\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p13.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p13.3.1" class="ltx_text">For every <math id="A3.SS2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the same conditional Poincaré estimate used in
the proof of <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1 (Derivative formula for 𝖴_𝖯𝖯). ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, together with
<math id="A3.SS2.p13.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\nabla g_{y})^{2}\preceq\beta\eta\,\nabla g_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⪯</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.317em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nabla g_{y})^{2}\preceq\beta\eta\,\nabla g_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> then give</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a^{\top}\mathrm{Cov}(g_{y}(W))a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a^{\top}\mathrm{Cov}(g_{y}(W))a</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\|\nabla g_{y}(W)\,a\|^{2}\leq\beta\eta\,a^{\top}\{I-\Sigma_{y}+\mathrm{Cov}(g_{y}(W))\}a\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\|\nabla g_{y}(W)\,a\|^{2}\leq\beta\eta\,a^{\top}\{I-\Sigma_{y}+\mathrm{Cov}(g_{y}(W))\}a\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p13.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p13.4.1" class="ltx_text">Rearranging proves (<a href="#A3.E13" title="Equation C.13 ‣ Lemma C.4 (Conditional gradient covariance bound). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.13</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition C.2 (Weighted half-turn estimate for affine functions). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A3.SS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, and let
<math id="A3.SS2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}\sim q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}\sim q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> be independent of
<math id="A3.SS2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W,P)\sim q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W,P)\sim q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>. We first apply the Duhamel formula to
identify the estimate that remains to be proved. Using, in order,
Jensen’s inequality in <math id="A3.SS2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}</annotation></semantics></math>,
(<a href="#A3.E12" title="Equation C.12 ‣ Lemma C.3 (Affine Duhamel formula). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.12</span></a>), the Bochner triangle inequality,
the contractivity of Gaussian momentum averaging and
<math id="A3.SS2.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A3.SS2.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\pi}\sin t\,\mathrm{d}t=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\pi}\sin t\,\mathrm{d}t=2</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{y})\ell_{a,y}\|_{L^{2}(q_{y})}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{y})\ell_{a,y}\|_{L^{2}(q_{y})}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{\widetilde{W}}\bigl\|\mathbb{E}_{P}[(I+\mathsf{T}_{\pi}^{y,\widetilde{W}})\ell_{a,y}]\bigr\|_{L^{2}(q_{y})}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{\widetilde{W}}\bigl\|\mathbb{E}_{P}[(I+\mathsf{T}_{\pi}^{y,\widetilde{W}})\ell_{a,y}]\bigr\|_{L^{2}(q_{y})}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{\widetilde{W}}\Bigl(\int_{0}^{\pi}\|\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{W}}k_{a,\widetilde{W}}\|_{L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))}\sin t\,\mathrm{d}t\Bigr)^{2}\leq 4\,\mathbb{E}_{W,\widetilde{W},P}k_{a,\widetilde{W}}^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>π</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{\widetilde{W}}\Bigl(\int_{0}^{\pi}\|\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{W}}k_{a,\widetilde{W}}\|_{L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))}\sin t\,\mathrm{d}t\Bigr)^{2}\leq 4\,\mathbb{E}_{W,\widetilde{W},P}k_{a,\widetilde{W}}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to bound the second moment on the right.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Conditional on <math id="A3.SS2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W,\widetilde{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W,\widetilde{W})</annotation></semantics></math>, a direct calculation with the
Gaussian momentum <math id="A3.SS2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, together with
<math id="A3.SS2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}g_{y}(W)=-\bar{w}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}g_{y}(W)=-\bar{w}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> from
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Conditional gradient covariance bound). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>, gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{P}[k_{a,\widetilde{W}}\mid W,\widetilde{W}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{P}[k_{a,\widetilde{W}}\mid W,\widetilde{W}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-a^{\top}\{g_{y}(W)-\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}g_{y}(W)\}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-a^{\top}\{g_{y}(W)-\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}g_{y}(W)\}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Var_{P}(k_{a,\widetilde{W}}\mid W,\widetilde{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">Var</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Var_{P}(k_{a,\widetilde{W}}\mid W,\widetilde{W})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=5\,[a^{\top}\{g_{y}(W)-g_{y}(\widetilde{W})\}]^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=5\,[a^{\top}\{g_{y}(W)-g_{y}(\widetilde{W})\}]^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">After averaging over the independent variables <math id="A3.SS2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS2.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}</annotation></semantics></math>, the conditional variance term contributes
<math id="A3.SS2.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\Var_{q_{y}}(a^{\top}g_{y}(W))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">Var</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\Var_{q_{y}}(a^{\top}g_{y}(W))</annotation></semantics></math>, while the squared conditional mean
contributes one more copy of the same variance. Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{W,\widetilde{W},P}k_{a,\widetilde{W}}^{2}=11\Var_{q_{y}}(a^{\top}g_{y}(W))\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">Var</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{W,\widetilde{W},P}k_{a,\widetilde{W}}^{2}=11\Var_{q_{y}}(a^{\top}g_{y}(W))\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Conditional gradient covariance bound). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{W,\widetilde{W},P}k_{a,\widetilde{W}}^{2}\leq C\beta\eta\,a^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{W,\widetilde{W},P}k_{a,\widetilde{W}}^{2}\leq C\beta\eta\,a^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p15.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p15.4.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the last estimate with the Duhamel bound proves
(<a href="#A3.E11" title="Equation C.11 ‣ Proposition C.2 (Weighted half-turn estimate for affine functions). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.11</span></a>). For the global
assertion, <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 2.1 (Geometry of the joint law). ‣ 2.2 Proximal augmentation and the restricted Gaussian oracle ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> gives
<math id="A3.SS2.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I-\Sigma_{y}\succeq\alpha\eta\,(1+\alpha\eta)^{-1}\,I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I-\Sigma_{y}\succeq\alpha\eta\,(1+\alpha\eta)^{-1}\,I</annotation></semantics></math>, so the stated
integrability condition implies <math id="A3.SS2.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math>. Its
conditional mean is zero. Applying the conditional inequality with
<math id="A3.SS2.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=a_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=a_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and integrating in <math id="A3.SS2.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> proves the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Proof of
<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>:
From affine estimates to the half-turn bound</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following proposition controls the part of the <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>-spectrum near
<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.5</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Interpolation bound on the <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>-spectral subspace
associated with <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\frac{1}{2},1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\frac{1}{2},1]</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq c</annotation></semantics></math>. If
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in\operatorname{ran}(\mathbf{1}_{[1/2,1]}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ran</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in\operatorname{ran}(\mathbf{1}_{[1/2,1]}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}))</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A3.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w\|^{2}\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}w\|\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{3}w\|\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w\|^{2}\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}w\|\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{3}w\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now prove <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We regard <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> as operators on
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math> and work with the spectral subspaces</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}\coloneqq\operatorname{ran}(\mathbf{1}_{[1/2,1]}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}))\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathcal{H}^{\prime}\coloneqq\operatorname{ran}(\mathbf{1}_{[-1/2,1/2)}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}))\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mi>ran</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mi>ran</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}\coloneqq\operatorname{ran}(\mathbf{1}_{[1/2,1]}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}))\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathcal{H}^{\prime}\coloneqq\operatorname{ran}(\mathbf{1}_{[-1/2,1/2)}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}))\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition C.5 (Interpolation bound on the 𝖴_𝖯𝖯-spectral subspace associated with [1/2,1]). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a> yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}v\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}v\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}v\|^{2}\leq C\,\|v\|\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}v\|\,\hskip 20.00003pt\forall v\in\mathcal{H}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.317em;" width="2.317em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}v\|^{2}\leq C\,\|v\|\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}v\|\,\hskip 20.00003pt\forall v\in\mathcal{H}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that by <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>,
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\rm gap}^{2}I\preceq\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\rm gap}^{2}I\preceq\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>.
Applying <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma D.4 (Comparison of positive operators). ‣ D.3 Comparison of positive operators ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a> with <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{A}=C^{-1/2}\,(\mathsf{T}^{*}\mathsf{T})^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝖳</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mi>𝖳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}=C^{-1/2}\,(\mathsf{T}^{*}\mathsf{T})^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}|_{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}|_{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=\gamma_{\rm gap}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=\gamma_{\rm gap}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=1</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}\coloneqq(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}|_{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳</mi><mo>≔</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}\coloneqq(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}|_{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>, gives a factor
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})</annotation></semantics></math>, up to a universal constant. Shrinking the
universal constant <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> in the assumption if necessary, we may suppose that
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq 1/16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq 1/16</annotation></semantics></math>. Then
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\rm gap}\leq 2\sqrt{\alpha\eta}\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\rm gap}\leq 2\sqrt{\alpha\eta}\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, so the additive constant is
absorbed by <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}v\|^{2}\leq C\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}v\|^{2}\,\hskip 20.00003pt\forall v\in\mathcal{H}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.317em;" width="2.317em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}v\|^{2}\leq C\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}v\|^{2}\,\hskip 20.00003pt\forall v\in\mathcal{H}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, on <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, no further spectral localization
is needed. Since <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> is a contraction,
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an isometry, and
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}\succeq\frac{3}{4}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}\succeq\frac{3}{4}I</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}v\|\leq 2\,\|v\|\leq 4\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}v\|\,\hskip 20.00003pt\forall v\in\mathcal{H}^{\prime}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.317em;" width="2.317em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}v\|\leq 2\,\|v\|\leq 4\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}v\|\,\hskip 20.00003pt\forall v\in\mathcal{H}^{\prime}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">For a general <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math>, decompose
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=v_{\mathcal{H}}+v_{\mathcal{H}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=v_{\mathcal{H}}+v_{\mathcal{H}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining the preceding two
estimates with <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a+b)^{2}\leq 2a^{2}+2b^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a+b)^{2}\leq 2a^{2}+2b^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and using that <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>
commutes with <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, proves
(<a href="#A2.E17" title="Equation B.17 ‣ Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.17</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We prove <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition C.5 (Interpolation bound on the 𝖴_𝖯𝖯-spectral subspace associated with [1/2,1]). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a> after the following preparatory results. The first
approximates <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w</annotation></semantics></math>, conditionally on <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, by a function
that is affine in the rescaled coordinate <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=(X-Y_{+})/\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=(X-Y_{+})/\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, so
that <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition C.2 (Weighted half-turn estimate for affine functions). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> applies. The second bounds the resulting
affine data by the gradients of <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w</annotation></semantics></math>, using the
derivative formula (<a href="#A3.E8" title="Equation C.8 ‣ Lemma C.1 (Derivative formula for 𝖴_𝖯𝖯). ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a>). Both results hold
for arbitrary functions in <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math>; the spectral
condition enters when we invert <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Recall from <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> the conditional law
<math id="A3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}\coloneqq\Law(W\mid Y_{+}=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}\coloneqq\Law(W\mid Y_{+}=y)</annotation></semantics></math>, its mean <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{w}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{w}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and covariance
<math id="A3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and that, conditionally on <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}=y</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A3.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=y+\sqrt{\eta}\,W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=y+\sqrt{\eta}\,W</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{-}=y+2\sqrt{\eta}\,W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{-}=y+2\sqrt{\eta}\,W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.6</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Conditional affine approximation and energy bound)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math>, and let
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{y}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[\nabla w(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{y}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[\nabla w(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]</annotation></semantics></math> denote the conditional mean of
the gradient. For <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>-almost every <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{y}(u)\coloneqq w(y+2\sqrt{\eta}u)-(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}w)(y)-2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{y}^{\top}(u-\bar{w}_{y})\,,\hskip 20.00003ptu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{y}(u)\coloneqq w(y+2\sqrt{\eta}u)-(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}w)(y)-2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{y}^{\top}(u-\bar{w}_{y})\,,\hskip 20.00003ptu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>-mean zero, the decomposition</span></p>
<table id="A3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w=2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{Y_{+}}^{\top}(W-\bar{w}_{Y_{+}})+e_{Y_{+}}(W)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w=2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{Y_{+}}^{\top}(W-\bar{w}_{Y_{+}})+e_{Y_{+}}(W)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">holds in <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math>, and, with</span></p>
<table id="A3.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}\coloneqq\|\nabla w\|^{2}-\int\|a_{y}\|^{2}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)=\mathbb{E}\|\nabla w(Y_{-})-a_{Y_{+}}\|^{2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}\coloneqq\|\nabla w\|^{2}-\int\|a_{y}\|^{2}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)=\mathbb{E}\|\nabla w(Y_{-})-a_{Y_{+}}\|^{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">one has</span></p>
<table id="A3.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[e_{Y_{+}}(W)^{2}]\leq 4\eta\mathcal{R}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[e_{Y_{+}}(W)^{2}]\leq 4\eta\mathcal{R}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, if <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq c</annotation></semantics></math> for a sufficiently small
universal constant <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{R}+\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\leq C\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\,\|\nabla w\|\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.039em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.039em">∥</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}+\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\leq C\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\,\|\nabla w\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w=w(Y_{-})-\mathbb{E}[w(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}]=w(Y_{-})-(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}w)(Y_{+})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w=w(Y_{-})-\mathbb{E}[w(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}]=w(Y_{-})-(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}w)(Y_{+})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Conditioning on <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}=y</annotation></semantics></math> and substituting <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{-}=y+2\sqrt{\eta}\,W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{-}=y+2\sqrt{\eta}\,W</annotation></semantics></math>
gives, for <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>-almost every <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w)(u)=w(y+2\sqrt{\eta}u)-(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}w)(y)\,,\hskip 20.00003ptu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w)(u)=w(y+2\sqrt{\eta}u)-(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}w)(y)\,,\hskip 20.00003ptu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">which is (<a href="#A3.E15" title="Equation C.15 ‣ Lemma C.6 (Conditional affine approximation and energy bound). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.15</span></a>). This function
belongs to <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(q_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(q_{y})</annotation></semantics></math> and has <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>-mean zero; since the
subtracted affine function is <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>-centered, <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> has
<math id="A3.SS3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>-mean zero as well.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">The coefficient <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen to center the gradient
of <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>: differentiating the preceding identity and averaging
under <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\nabla_{u}(\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w)(u)\,q_{y}(\mathrm{d}u)=2\sqrt{\eta}\,\mathbb{E}[\nabla w(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]=2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{y}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\nabla_{u}(\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w)(u)\,q_{y}(\mathrm{d}u)=2\sqrt{\eta}\,\mathbb{E}[\nabla w(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]=2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{y}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">and hence</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{u}e_{y}(W)=2\sqrt{\eta}\,\{\nabla w(Y_{-})-a_{y}\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{u}e_{y}(W)=2\sqrt{\eta}\,\{\nabla w(Y_{-})-a_{y}\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> has Poincaré constant at most <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[e_{y}(W)^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]\leq\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla_{u}e_{y}(W)\|^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]=4\eta\,\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla w(Y_{-})-a_{y}\|^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[e_{y}(W)^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]\leq\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla_{u}e_{y}(W)\|^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]=4\eta\,\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla w(Y_{-})-a_{y}\|^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Integrating in <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and expanding the square using the definition of
<math id="A3.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> proves (<a href="#A3.E17" title="Equation C.17 ‣ Lemma C.6 (Conditional affine approximation and energy bound). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.17</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We turn to the energy estimate. We may assume <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall that
<math id="A3.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g_{y}(u)=\sqrt{\eta}\,\nabla V(y+\sqrt{\eta}u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.317em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{y}(u)=\sqrt{\eta}\,\nabla V(y+\sqrt{\eta}u)</annotation></semantics></math>, so that
<math id="A3.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla V(X)=\eta^{-1/2}g_{y}(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V(X)=\eta^{-1/2}g_{y}(W)</annotation></semantics></math>, and that
<math id="A3.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}(W,g_{y}(W)\mid Y_{+}=y)=I-\Sigma_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}(W,g_{y}(W)\mid Y_{+}=y)=I-\Sigma_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> by
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Conditional gradient covariance bound). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>. The decomposition
(<a href="#A3.E15" title="Equation C.15 ‣ Lemma C.6 (Conditional affine approximation and energy bound). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.15</span></a>) therefore gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}(w(Y_{-}),\nabla V(X)\mid Y_{+}=y)=2(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}+\eta^{-1/2}\varepsilon_{y}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\varepsilon_{y}\coloneqq\mathrm{Cov}(e_{y}(W),g_{y}(W)\mid Y_{+}=y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}(w(Y_{-}),\nabla V(X)\mid Y_{+}=y)=2(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}+\eta^{-1/2}\varepsilon_{y}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\varepsilon_{y}\coloneqq\mathrm{Cov}(e_{y}(W),g_{y}(W)\mid Y_{+}=y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this into (<a href="#A3.E8" title="Equation C.8 ‣ Lemma C.1 (Derivative formula for 𝖴_𝖯𝖯). ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w](y)=\nabla w(y)-a_{y}+2(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}+\eta^{-1/2}\varepsilon_{y}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w](y)=\nabla w(y)-a_{y}+2(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}+\eta^{-1/2}\varepsilon_{y}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Conditional Cauchy–Schwarz and
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Conditional gradient covariance bound). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a> give, for every
<math id="A3.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\varepsilon_{y}^{\top}v|^{2}\leq C\beta\eta\,\mathbb{E}[e_{y}(W)^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]\,v^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})v\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\varepsilon_{y}^{\top}v|^{2}\leq C\beta\eta\,\mathbb{E}[e_{y}(W)^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]\,v^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})v\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">We will also use</span></p>
<table id="A3.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\preceq I-\Sigma_{y}\preceq\beta\eta I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\preceq I-\Sigma_{y}\preceq\beta\eta I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">The two-sided bound in
<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, together with the fact that
<math id="A3.SS3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> fixes constants, gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})^{2}\preceq 3\,(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})^{2}\preceq 3\,(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">on <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="A3.SS3.p8.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{y}=(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\nabla w)(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{y}=(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\nabla w)(y)</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> acting coordinatewise,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{R}=\bigl\langle\nabla w,(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})\nabla w\bigr\rangle\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\int\|\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\|^{2}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\leq 3\mathcal{R}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.000em">,</mo><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}=\bigl\langle\nabla w,(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})\nabla w\bigr\rangle\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\int\|\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\|^{2}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\leq 3\mathcal{R}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now control <math id="A3.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and the affine energy simultaneously.
Take the <math id="A3.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> inner product of
(<a href="#A3.E19" title="Equation C.19 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.19</span></a>) with the vector field
<math id="A3.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\mapsto\nabla w(y)+a_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\mapsto\nabla w(y)+a_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\{\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\}^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)=\mathcal{R}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\{\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\}^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)=\mathcal{R}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain the exact identity</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}+4\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}+4\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex62.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int[\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w](y)^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int[\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w](y)^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt-2\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})\{\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt-2\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})\{\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt-\eta^{-1/2}\int\varepsilon_{y}^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt-\eta^{-1/2}\int\varepsilon_{y}^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We bound the three terms on the right separately. For the first,
conditional Jensen gives <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\|a_{y}\|^{2}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\leq\|\nabla w\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\|a_{y}\|^{2}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\leq\|\nabla w\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and hence</span></p>
<table id="A3.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Bigl\lvert\int[\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w](y)^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\rvert\leq 2\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\,\|\nabla w\|\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.039em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.039em">∥</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl\lvert\int[\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w](y)^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\rvert\leq 2\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\,\|\nabla w\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the second, Cauchy–Schwarz,
(<a href="#A3.E21" title="Equation C.21 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.21</span></a>), and
(<a href="#A3.E22" title="Equation C.22 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.22</span></a>) give</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\,\Bigl|\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})\{\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr|\leq C\sqrt{\beta\eta}\,\mathcal{R}^{1/2}\,\Bigl\{\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\}^{1/2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\,\Bigl|\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})\{\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr|\leq C\sqrt{\beta\eta}\,\mathcal{R}^{1/2}\,\Bigl\{\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\}^{1/2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, using the pointwise identity
<math id="A3.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla w(y)+a_{y}=\{\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\}+2a_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla w(y)+a_{y}=\{\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\}+2a_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>,
(<a href="#A3.E21" title="Equation C.21 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.21</span></a>) and
(<a href="#A3.E22" title="Equation C.22 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.22</span></a>) imply</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\leq C\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}+8\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\leq C\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}+8\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">Using (<a href="#A3.E20" title="Equation C.20 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.20</span></a>), Cauchy–Schwarz in <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>,
(<a href="#A3.E17" title="Equation C.17 ‣ Lemma C.6 (Conditional affine approximation and energy bound). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.17</span></a>), and
(<a href="#A3.E26" title="Equation C.26 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.26</span></a>), we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\eta^{-1/2}\,\Bigl|\int\varepsilon_{y}^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" lspace="0.150em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta^{-1/2}\,\Bigl|\int\varepsilon_{y}^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt\leq C\sqrt{\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}}\,\Bigl\{\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}+\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\}^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt\leq C\sqrt{\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}}\,\Bigl\{\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}+\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\}^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt\leq C\sqrt{\beta\eta}\,\mathcal{R}^{1/2}\,\Bigl\{\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\}^{1/2}+C\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt\leq C\sqrt{\beta\eta}\,\mathcal{R}^{1/2}\,\Bigl\{\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\}^{1/2}+C\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting these three estimates into
(<a href="#A3.E23" title="Equation C.23 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.23</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}+4\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}+4\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex66.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\,\|\nabla w\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.039em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\,\|\nabla w\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt+C\sqrt{\beta\eta}\,\mathcal{R}^{1/2}\Bigl\{\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\}^{1/2}+C\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt+C\sqrt{\beta\eta}\,\mathcal{R}^{1/2}\Bigl\{\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\}^{1/2}+C\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">For sufficiently small universal <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, the last two terms
are absorbed into the left-hand side. This proves (<a href="#A3.E18" title="Equation C.18 ‣ Lemma C.6 (Conditional affine approximation and energy bound). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.18</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition C.5 (Interpolation bound on the 𝖴_𝖯𝖯-spectral subspace associated with [1/2,1]). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Choose a small enough universal constant in the hypothesis, if necessary, so
that <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma C.6 (Conditional affine approximation and energy bound). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a> applies. On
<math id="A3.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{ran}(\mathbf{1}_{[1/2,1]}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ran</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{ran}(\mathbf{1}_{[1/2,1]}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}))</annotation></semantics></math>, the operator
<math id="A3.SS3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded.
Applying (<a href="#A2.E13" title="Equation B.13 ‣ Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.13</span></a>) first to
<math id="A3.SS3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}w</annotation></semantics></math> and then to
<math id="A3.SS3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{\eta}\,\|\nabla w\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{\eta}\,\|\nabla w\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}w\|\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}w\|\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}w\|\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}w\|\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{\eta}\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{\eta}\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{3}w\|\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{3}w\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here, the final inequality in each line follows by spectral calculus
on <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\frac{1}{2},1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\frac{1}{2},1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Decompose <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w</annotation></semantics></math> according to
(<a href="#A3.E15" title="Equation C.15 ‣ Lemma C.6 (Conditional affine approximation and energy bound). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.15</span></a>). The affine part has
coefficient <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition C.2 (Weighted half-turn estimate for affine functions). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>, <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\|\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\|\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>
applied to the error term, and <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r+s)^{2}\leq 2r^{2}+2s^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r+s)^{2}\leq 2r^{2}+2s^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> give</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C\beta\eta^{2}\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)+C\,\mathbb{E}[e_{Y_{+}}(W)^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C\beta\eta^{2}\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)+C\,\mathbb{E}[e_{Y_{+}}(W)^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C\eta\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\,\|\nabla w\|\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.039em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.317em">∥</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C\eta\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\,\|\nabla w\|\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last line uses <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma C.6 (Conditional affine approximation and energy bound). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a>. Finally,
(<a href="#A3.E28" title="Equation C.28 ‣ Proof of . ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.28</span></a>) gives (<a href="#A3.E14" title="Equation C.14 ‣ Proposition C.5 (Interpolation bound on the 𝖴_𝖯𝖯-spectral subspace associated with [1/2,1]). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.14</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Technical tools</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix collects the functional analysis and log-concavity tools
used throughout the process and convergence analyses.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Hilbert space and Markov operator conventions</h3>

<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Hilbert space notation)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> be a probability measure. The real Hilbert space
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math> consists of equivalence classes of measurable functions
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int f^{2}\,\mathrm{d}\zeta&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int f^{2}\,\mathrm{d}\zeta&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Its inner product and
norm are</p>
<table id="A4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle f,g\rangle_{L^{2}(\zeta)}\coloneqq\int fg\,\mathrm{d}\zeta\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\|f\|_{L^{2}(\zeta)}\coloneqq\langle f,f\rangle_{L^{2}(\zeta)}^{1/2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle f,g\rangle_{L^{2}(\zeta)}\coloneqq\int fg\,\mathrm{d}\zeta\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\|f\|_{L^{2}(\zeta)}\coloneqq\langle f,f\rangle_{L^{2}(\zeta)}^{1/2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We write</p>
<table id="A4.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{0}^{2}(\zeta)\coloneqq\Bigl\{f\in L^{2}(\zeta):\int f\,\mathrm{d}\zeta=0\Bigr\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{0}^{2}(\zeta)\coloneqq\Bigl\{f\in L^{2}(\zeta):\int f\,\mathrm{d}\zeta=0\Bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta=\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta=\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we abbreviate the inner product and norm by
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle f,g\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle f,g\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Two functions equal <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>-almost everywhere represent the same
vector. A closed linear subspace <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}\subseteq L^{2}(\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}\subseteq L^{2}(\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math>
has orthogonal complement
<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{\perp}\coloneqq\{g:\langle f,g\rangle=0\text{ for all }f\in\mathcal{M}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{\perp}\coloneqq\{g:\langle f,g\rangle=0\text{ for all }f\in\mathcal{M}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Its orthogonal projection is the unique bounded operator
<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> for which <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}_{\mathcal{M}}f\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}_{\mathcal{M}}f\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f-\mathsf{P}_{\mathcal{M}}f\in\mathcal{M}^{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f-\mathsf{P}_{\mathcal{M}}f\in\mathcal{M}^{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">All operators in the convergence analysis are bounded linear operators
on the indicated Hilbert spaces unless explicitly stated otherwise.
The adjoint <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖫</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is characterized by
<math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathsf{L}f,g\rangle=\langle f,\mathsf{L}^{*}g\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖫</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathsf{L}f,g\rangle=\langle f,\mathsf{L}^{*}g\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
An operator is self-adjoint if <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}=\mathsf{L}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝖫</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}=\mathsf{L}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, a contraction
if <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathsf{L}f\|\leq\|f\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{L}f\|\leq\|f\|</annotation></semantics></math>, and unitary if it is onto and preserves
norms. A self-adjoint involution, meaning <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}^{2}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝖫</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}^{2}=I</annotation></semantics></math>, is
unitary. For self-adjoint operators <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}_{1},\mathsf{L}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}_{1},\mathsf{L}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{L}_{1}\preceq\mathsf{L}_{2}\hskip 10.00002pt\Longleftrightarrow\hskip 10.00002pt\langle f,(\mathsf{L}_{2}-\mathsf{L}_{1})f\rangle\geq 0\hskip 10.00002pt\text{for every }f" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>f</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext>for every </mtext><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}_{1}\preceq\mathsf{L}_{2}\hskip 10.00002pt\Longleftrightarrow\hskip 10.00002pt\langle f,(\mathsf{L}_{2}-\mathsf{L}_{1})f\rangle\geq 0\hskip 10.00002pt\text{for every }f</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">is the Loewner order. If <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is self-adjoint, the
spectral theorem defines <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\mathsf{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\mathsf{L})</annotation></semantics></math> for bounded Borel functions
<math id="A4.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>; in particular <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{E}(\mathsf{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{E}(\mathsf{L})</annotation></semantics></math> is the orthogonal
projection onto the spectral set <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, and a non-negative operator has
a unique non-negative square root.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Markov operators and density evolution)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}(z,\mathrm{d}z^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}(z,\mathrm{d}z^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> be a Markov kernel preserving <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>. Its
Markov operator on observables is</p>
<table id="A4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{K}f)(z)\coloneqq\int f(z^{\prime})\,\mathcal{K}(z,\mathrm{d}z^{\prime})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{K}f)(z)\coloneqq\int f(z^{\prime})\,\mathcal{K}(z,\mathrm{d}z^{\prime})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">It is a contraction on <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math>. Its adjoint
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> governs density evolution: if a law has density <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> with
respect to <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>, then its density after one step is <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}^{*}h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}^{*}h</annotation></semantics></math>.
Constants are fixed by both operators.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\ll\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\ll\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> has density <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\chi^{2}(P\|\zeta)=\|h-1\|_{\zeta}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}(P\|\zeta)=\|h-1\|_{\zeta}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Consequently, an operator norm bound for <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}</annotation></semantics></math> on
<math id="A4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{0}^{2}(\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{0}^{2}(\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math> gives the same bound for its adjoint
<math id="A4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence gives <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> contraction.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Strong log-concavity and covariance bounds</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We repeatedly use the following standard consequences of
Bakry–Émery curvature. If a probability measure
<math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu(\mathrm{d}z)\propto e^{-W(z)}\,\mathrm{d}z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(\mathrm{d}z)\propto e^{-W(z)}\,\mathrm{d}z</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies
<math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}W\succeq mI" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}W\succeq mI</annotation></semantics></math>, then, for smooth <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Var_{\nu}(f)\leq\frac{1}{m}\,\mathbb{E}_{\nu}\|\nabla f\|^{2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">Var</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Var_{\nu}(f)\leq\frac{1}{m}\,\mathbb{E}_{\nu}\|\nabla f\|^{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the log-Sobolev inequality with constant
<math id="A4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/m</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, every <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> obeys Gaussian
concentration</p>
<table id="A4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\{f-\mathbb{E}f\geq t\}\leq\exp\Bigl(-\frac{mt^{2}}{2L^{2}}\Bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\{f-\mathbb{E}f\geq t\}\leq\exp\Bigl(-\frac{mt^{2}}{2L^{2}}\Bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">These statements follow from the Bakry–Émery criterion; see, for
example, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, Chapters 4 and 5]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Two-sided covariance bound)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu(\mathrm{d}z)\propto e^{-W(z)}\,\mathrm{d}z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(\mathrm{d}z)\propto e^{-W(z)}\,\mathrm{d}z</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="A4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mI\preceq\nabla^{2}W(z)\preceq LI\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mI\preceq\nabla^{2}W(z)\preceq LI\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="A4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{-1}I\preceq\mathrm{Cov}_{\nu}(Z)\preceq m^{-1}I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{-1}I\preceq\mathrm{Cov}_{\nu}(Z)\preceq m^{-1}I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The upper bound is the Brascamp–Lieb
inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, Chapter 4]</cite> applied to linear functions. The lower
bound follows from the Cramér–Rao inequality for the location family
generated by <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}_{\nu}(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}_{\nu}(Z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\succeq\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{\nu}\nabla^{2}W(Z)\bigr)^{-1}\succeq L^{-1}I\,.\qed" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⪰</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\succeq\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{\nu}\nabla^{2}W(Z)\bigr)^{-1}\succeq L^{-1}I\,.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hessian of the augmented marginal.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{x}_{y}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[X\mid Y=y]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{x}_{y}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[X\mid Y=y]</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{y}\coloneqq\eta^{-1}\,\mathrm{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{y}\coloneqq\eta^{-1}\,\mathrm{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)</annotation></semantics></math>, as in the normalized
coordinates of Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>. Differentiating the
log-density of <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla U_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}(y-\bar{x}_{y})\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\nabla^{2}U_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}(I-\Sigma_{y})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla U_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}(y-\bar{x}_{y})\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\nabla^{2}U_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}(I-\Sigma_{y})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The conditional potential in <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> has Hessian between
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha+\eta^{-1})I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha+\eta^{-1})I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta+\eta^{-1})I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta+\eta^{-1})I</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying
<a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3 (Two-sided covariance bound). ‣ D.2 Strong log-concavity and covariance bounds ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> in (<a href="#A4.E10" title="Equation D.10 ‣ Hessian of the augmented marginal. ‣ D.2 Strong log-concavity and covariance bounds ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.10</span></a>) gives
(<a href="#S2.E13" title="Equation 2.13 ‣ Item (ii) ‣ Proposition 2.1 (Geometry of the joint law). ‣ 2.2 Proximal augmentation and the restricted Gaussian oracle ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.13</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Comparison of positive operators</h3>

<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.4</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Comparison of positive operators)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A},\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖡</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A},\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> be bounded positive semidefinite self-adjoint
operators on a Hilbert space <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, and suppose that for <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\geq m&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\geq m&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;mI\preceq\mathsf{B}\preceq MI" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;mI\preceq\mathsf{B}\preceq MI</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume that, for every <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathsf{A}v\|^{2}\leq\|v\|\,\|\mathsf{B}v\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{A}v\|^{2}\leq\|v\|\,\|\mathsf{B}v\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, for <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\coloneqq\frac{M}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\coloneqq\frac{M}{m}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}^{2}\preceq\bigl(1+\frac{\log K}{\pi}\bigr)\,\mathsf{B}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖡</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}^{2}\preceq\bigl(1+\frac{\log K}{\pi}\bigr)\,\mathsf{B}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By replacing</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{A}\leftarrow m^{-1/2}\mathsf{A}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{B}\leftarrow m^{-1}\mathsf{B}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝖡</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}\leftarrow m^{-1/2}\mathsf{A}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{B}\leftarrow m^{-1}\mathsf{B}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">we may assume without loss of generality that <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\preceq\mathsf{B}\preceq KI" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\preceq\mathsf{B}\preceq KI</annotation></semantics></math>.
For non-zero <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle v,\mathsf{A}^{2}v\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle v,\mathsf{A}^{2}v\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle\mathsf{B}^{1/2}v,\mathsf{B}^{-1/2}\mathsf{A}^{2}\mathsf{B}^{-1/2}\mathsf{B}^{1/2}v\rangle\leq\|\mathsf{B}^{-1/2}\mathsf{A}^{2}\mathsf{B}^{-1/2}\|\,\langle v,\mathsf{B}v\rangle=\|\mathsf{A}\mathsf{B}^{-1}\mathsf{A}\|\,\langle v,\mathsf{B}v\rangle\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><msup><mi>𝖡</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝖡</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>𝖡</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>𝖡</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>v</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>𝖡</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>𝖡</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.317em">∥</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mi>v</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>𝖠𝖡</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.317em">∥</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mi>v</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle\mathsf{B}^{1/2}v,\mathsf{B}^{-1/2}\mathsf{A}^{2}\mathsf{B}^{-1/2}\mathsf{B}^{1/2}v\rangle\leq\|\mathsf{B}^{-1/2}\mathsf{A}^{2}\mathsf{B}^{-1/2}\|\,\langle v,\mathsf{B}v\rangle=\|\mathsf{A}\mathsf{B}^{-1}\mathsf{A}\|\,\langle v,\mathsf{B}v\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Also,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathsf{A}\mathsf{B}^{-1}\mathsf{A}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖠𝖡</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖠</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathsf{A}\mathsf{B}^{-1}\mathsf{A}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Bigl\lVert\frac{2}{\pi}\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathsf{A}(t^{2}I+\mathsf{B}^{2})^{-1}\mathsf{A}\,\mathrm{d}t\Bigr\rVert\leq\frac{2}{\pi}\int_{0}^{\infty}\|\mathsf{A}(t^{2}I+\mathsf{B}^{2})^{-1}\mathsf{A}\|\,\mathrm{d}t\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝖡</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝖡</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖠</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Bigl\lVert\frac{2}{\pi}\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathsf{A}(t^{2}I+\mathsf{B}^{2})^{-1}\mathsf{A}\,\mathrm{d}t\Bigr\rVert\leq\frac{2}{\pi}\int_{0}^{\infty}\|\mathsf{A}(t^{2}I+\mathsf{B}^{2})^{-1}\mathsf{A}\|\,\mathrm{d}t\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, by hypothesis,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathsf{A}(t^{2}I+\mathsf{B}^{2})^{-1}\mathsf{A}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝖡</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖠</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathsf{A}(t^{2}I+\mathsf{B}^{2})^{-1}\mathsf{A}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\|(t^{2}I+\mathsf{B}^{2})^{-1/2}\mathsf{A}^{2}(t^{2}I+\mathsf{B}^{2})^{-1/2}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝖡</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝖡</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|(t^{2}I+\mathsf{B}^{2})^{-1/2}\mathsf{A}^{2}(t^{2}I+\mathsf{B}^{2})^{-1/2}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sup_{v\in\mathcal{H}\setminus\{0\}}\frac{\|\mathsf{A}(t^{2}I+\mathsf{B}^{2})^{-1/2}v\|^{2}}{\|v\|^{2}}=\sup_{u\in\mathcal{H}\setminus\{0\}}\frac{\|\mathsf{A}u\|^{2}}{t^{2}\,\|u\|^{2}+\|\mathsf{B}u\|^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.280em" minsize="1.280em">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo maxsize="1.280em" minsize="1.280em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.280em" minsize="1.280em">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo maxsize="1.280em" minsize="1.280em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sup_{v\in\mathcal{H}\setminus\{0\}}\frac{\|\mathsf{A}(t^{2}I+\mathsf{B}^{2})^{-1/2}v\|^{2}}{\|v\|^{2}}=\sup_{u\in\mathcal{H}\setminus\{0\}}\frac{\|\mathsf{A}u\|^{2}}{t^{2}\,\|u\|^{2}+\|\mathsf{B}u\|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sup_{u\in\mathcal{H}\setminus\{0\}}\frac{\|u\|\,\|\mathsf{B}u\|}{t^{2}\,\|u\|^{2}+\|\mathsf{B}u\|^{2}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.280em" minsize="1.280em">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo maxsize="1.280em" minsize="1.280em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sup_{u\in\mathcal{H}\setminus\{0\}}\frac{\|u\|\,\|\mathsf{B}u\|}{t^{2}\,\|u\|^{2}+\|\mathsf{B}u\|^{2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Setting <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\coloneqq\|\mathsf{B}u\|/\|u\|\in[1,K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\coloneqq\|\mathsf{B}u\|/\|u\|\in[1,K]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathsf{A}(t^{2}I+\mathsf{B}^{2})^{-1}\mathsf{A}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝖡</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖠</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathsf{A}(t^{2}I+\mathsf{B}^{2})^{-1}\mathsf{A}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sup_{r\in[1,K]}\frac{r}{t^{2}+r^{2}}=\begin{cases}1/(t^{2}+1)\,,&amp;t&lt;1\,,\\
1/(2t)\,,&amp;t\in[1,K]\,,\\
K/(t^{2}+K^{2})\,,&amp;t&gt;K\,.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sup_{r\in[1,K]}\frac{r}{t^{2}+r^{2}}=\begin{cases}1/(t^{2}+1)\,,&amp;t&lt;1\,,\\
1/(2t)\,,&amp;t\in[1,K]\,,\\
K/(t^{2}+K^{2})\,,&amp;t&gt;K\,.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathsf{A}\mathsf{B}^{-1}\mathsf{A}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖠𝖡</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖠</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathsf{A}\mathsf{B}^{-1}\mathsf{A}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{2}{\pi}\,\Bigl(\int_{0}^{1}\frac{1}{t^{2}+1}\,\mathrm{d}t+\int_{1}^{K}\frac{1}{2t}\,\mathrm{d}t+\int_{K}^{\infty}\frac{K}{t^{2}+K^{2}}\,\mathrm{d}t\Bigr)=1+\frac{\log K}{\pi}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>K</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{2}{\pi}\,\Bigl(\int_{0}^{1}\frac{1}{t^{2}+1}\,\mathrm{d}t+\int_{1}^{K}\frac{1}{2t}\,\mathrm{d}t+\int_{K}^{\infty}\frac{K}{t^{2}+K^{2}}\,\mathrm{d}t\Bigr)=1+\frac{\log K}{\pi}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The logarithmic dependence on <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma D.4 (Comparison of positive operators). ‣ D.3 Comparison of positive operators ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a> is sharp in general.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark D.5</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, take <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}=L^{2}([1,K],\mathrm{d}x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}=L^{2}([1,K],\mathrm{d}x)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{A}f(x)\coloneqq(\pi\,(K-1))^{-1/2}\int_{1}^{K}f(y)\,\mathrm{d}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}f(x)\coloneqq(\pi\,(K-1))^{-1/2}\int_{1}^{K}f(y)\,\mathrm{d}y</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}f(x)\coloneqq xf(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}f(x)\coloneqq xf(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, by the classical integral Carlson inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathsf{A}f\|^{2}=\frac{1}{\pi}\,\Bigl(\int_{1}^{K}f(y)\,\mathrm{d}y\Bigr)^{2}\leq\|f\|\,\|\mathsf{B}f\|\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{A}f\|^{2}=\frac{1}{\pi}\,\Bigl(\int_{1}^{K}f(y)\,\mathrm{d}y\Bigr)^{2}\leq\|f\|\,\|\mathsf{B}f\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Thus, the hypotheses of <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma D.4 (Comparison of positive operators). ‣ D.3 Comparison of positive operators ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a> are met.
If we take <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)\coloneqq 1/x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)\coloneqq 1/x</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathsf{A}f\|^{2}=(\log K)^{2}/\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{A}f\|^{2}=(\log K)^{2}/\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle f,\mathsf{B}f\rangle=\log K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle f,\mathsf{B}f\rangle=\log K</annotation></semantics></math>, so the best possible constant in <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma D.4 (Comparison of positive operators). ‣ D.3 Comparison of positive operators ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a> can be no better than <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{1,(\log K)/\pi\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{1,(\log K)/\pi\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the maximum with <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> arises from the trivial case <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}=\mathsf{B}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖡</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}=\mathsf{B}=I</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
